1
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:29,110
Mozart!

2
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:40,580
Mozart!

3
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:43,370
Forgive your assassin!

4
00:00:43,910 --> 00:00:47,540
I confess, I killed you!

5
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,790
Si, I killed you, Mozart.

6
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:58,340
Mozart, piet? Forgive your assassin!

7
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:01,930
Forgive me, Mozart!

8
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:07,850
Signore Salieri, open the door, be good now!

9
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:14,740
Signore, we have something special for you.Something you're going to love.

10
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:20,820
Mmm! Is that good!

11
00:01:23,330 --> 00:01:25,830
Signore, believe me.

12
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,420
this is the most delicious thing I ever ate in my life!

13
00:01:31,290 --> 00:01:33,380
Really, you don't know what you're miss

14
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:43,510
All right, that's enough! Open the door.

15
00:01:46,890 --> 00:01:50,190
Signore, if you don't open this door...

16
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:53,320
we're gonna leave nothing for you.

17
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:56,690
And I'm never gonna come see you again!

18
00:04:55,790 --> 00:04:58,000
Good morning, Father.

19
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:29,410
Herr Salieri?

20
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:05,860
Leave me alone.

21
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:15,040
I cannot leave alone a soul in pain.

22
00:06:16,450 --> 00:06:18,290
Do you know who I am?

23
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:22,710
That makes no difference.

24
00:06:23,170 --> 00:06:26,130
All men are equal in God's eyes.

25
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:32,720
Are they?

26
00:06:33,550 --> 00:06:36,220
Offer me your confession.

27
00:06:39,310 --> 00:06:42,400
I can offer you God's forgiveness.

28
00:06:46,730 --> 00:06:49,650
How well are you trained in music?

29
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:56,080
I know a little. I studied it in my youth.

30
00:06:56,990 --> 00:06:59,580
-Where? -Here in Vienna.

31
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:03,830
Oh! Then you must know this.

32
00:07:12,430 --> 00:07:14,850
I can't say that I do.

33
00:07:16,010 --> 00:07:17,310
What is it?

34
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:21,640
It was a very popular tune in its day.

35
00:07:21,850 --> 00:07:23,100
I wrote it.

36
00:07:25,270 --> 00:07:27,520
Here, how about this?

37
00:07:30,650 --> 00:07:34,280
This one brought down the house when we played it.

38
00:08:19,490 --> 00:08:21,240
Well?

39
00:08:23,870 --> 00:08:27,580
I regret it is not too familiar.

40
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:30,050
Can you recall no melody of mine?

41
00:08:31,090 --> 00:08:34,340
I was the most famous composer in Europe.

42
00:08:34,550 --> 00:08:37,090
I wrote 40 operas alone.

43
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:43,100
Here! What about this one?

44
00:08:58,870 --> 00:09:03,370
Yes, I know that! That's charming!

45
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:06,580
I'm sorry, I didn't know you wrote that.

46
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,250
I didn't.

47
00:09:16,090 --> 00:09:22,720
That was Mozart. Wolfgang...

48
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:26,730
Amadeus Mozart.

49
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:31,570
The man you accuse yourself of killing.

50
00:09:35,070 --> 00:09:37,150
You've heard that?

51
00:09:37,450 --> 00:09:39,410
Is it true?

52
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:51,130
For God's sake, my son...

53
00:09:53,250 --> 00:09:58,010
if you have something to confess, do it now.

54
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:01,140
Give yourself some peace.

55
00:10:04,890 --> 00:10:10,100
He...was my idol.

56
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:15,400
Mozart.

57
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:20,200
I can't think of a time when I didn't know his name.

58
00:10:20,410 --> 00:10:22,200
I was playing games...

59
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:26,700
when he was playing music for kings and emperors.

60
00:10:26,910 --> 00:10:29,540
Even the pope in Rome.

61
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:35,800
I admit, I was jealous...

62
00:10:36,130 --> 00:10:39,340
when I heard the tales they told about him.

63
00:10:39,550 --> 00:10:41,930
Not of the brilliant little prodigy...

64
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:47,020
but of his father, who had taught him everything.

65
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:50,560
My father, he did not care for music.

66
00:10:51,230 --> 00:10:52,690
When I told him...

67
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:56,440
how I wished I could be like Mozart...

68
00:10:56,650 --> 00:11:01,070
he would say, "Why? Do you want to be a trained monkey?

69
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:06,240
You'd like me to drag you around, doing tricks like a circus freak?"

70
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,250
How could I tell him...

71
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:16,250
what music meant to me?

72
00:11:30,350 --> 00:11:33,560
While my father prayed earnestly to God...

73
00:11:33,770 --> 00:11:36,440
to protect commerce...

74
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:41,190
I would offer up...secretly...

75
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:44,950
the proudest prayer a boy could think of.

76
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:49,450
Lord, make me a great composer.

77
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:56,630
Let me celebrate your glory through music...and be celebrated myself.

78
00:11:58,090 --> 00:12:00,760
Make me famous through the world. deer God.

79
00:12:01,010 --> 00:12:03,630
Make me immortal.

80
00:12:04,470 --> 00:12:06,430
After I die...

81
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:11,470
let people speak my name with love for what I wrote.

82
00:12:12,810 --> 00:12:18,980
In return...I will give you my chastity...

83
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:21,570
my industry...

84
00:12:23,530 --> 00:12:26,950
my deepest humility, every hour of my life.

85
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:34,750
And do you know what happened?

86
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,080
A miracle!

87
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:57,600
My life changed forever.

88
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:02,110
I knew God had arranged it all.

89
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:05,530
That was obvious. One minute I was a frustrated boy...

90
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:09,620
in an obscure little town. The next I was here...

91
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:12,950
in Vienna, city of musicians...

92
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:17,830
and Emperor Joseph, the musical king.

93
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:23,000
In a few years, I was his court composer. Isn't that incredible?

94
00:13:23,210 --> 00:13:31,350
Every night I sat with the emperor of Austria...playing duets with him...correcting the royal sight-reading.

95
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:38,230
Actually, the man had no ear at all.

96
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:41,610
But what did it matter?

97
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:45,190
He adored my music.

98
00:13:45,990 --> 00:13:47,860
Tell me....

99
00:13:48,110 --> 00:13:50,490
If you had been me...

100
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:55,620
wouldn't you have thought God had accepted your vow?

101
00:13:57,410 --> 00:13:59,750
And believe me, I honored it.

102
00:14:00,210 --> 00:14:02,670
I was a model of virtue.

103
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:05,210
I kept my hands off women.

104
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:09,880
I worked hours every day teaching students, many for free!

105
00:14:10,090 --> 00:14:15,270
Sitting on endless committees to help poor musicians.

106
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,140
Work, that was all my life.

107
00:14:18,350 --> 00:14:20,440
And it was wonderful.

108
00:14:20,730 --> 00:14:23,190
Everybody liked me.

109
00:14:25,230 --> 00:14:27,400
I liked myself.

110
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:32,950
Until he came.

111
00:14:34,950 --> 00:14:39,290
He came to Vienna to play some of his music...

112
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:46,050
at the residence of the Prince Archbishop of Salzburg.

113
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:50,720
Eagerly, I went there to seek him out.

114
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:55,930
That night...

115
00:14:57,680 --> 00:14:59,980
changed my life.

116
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:06,820
As I wandered through the salon...

117
00:15:07,070 --> 00:15:09,780
I played a little game with myself.

118
00:15:09,990 --> 00:15:14,410
This man had written his first concerto at the age of 4...

119
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:19,580
his first symphony at 7, a full-scale opera at 12!

120
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,250
Did it show?

121
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:29,630
Is talent like that...written on the face?

122
00:15:31,010 --> 00:15:33,510
Which one of them...

123
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:37,510
could he be?

124
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,600
Mozart is not here.

125
00:17:47,850 --> 00:17:49,100
-Stop it! -I am.

126
00:17:49,310 --> 00:17:51,650
-Stop it! -I am stopping it.

127
00:17:51,900 --> 00:18:00,660
I am! I'm stopping it. Slowly. There. You see? I've stopped.

128
00:18:00,870 --> 00:18:02,870
-Now we're going back. -No!

129
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,750
Yes! You don't know where you are.

130
00:18:05,950 --> 00:18:08,500
Here, everything goes backwards.

131
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:13,840
People walk and dance and sing and even talk backwards.

132
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:18,880
-That's stupid. -Why? People fart backwards.

133
00:18:20,890 --> 00:18:22,760
Ssa-ym-ssik!

134
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,850
Ssa-ym-ssik!

135
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,430
Yes, you are. You are very sick.

136
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:31,020
No! Say it backwards, shitwit!

137
00:18:31,650 --> 00:18:33,520
Ssa-ym-ssik.

138
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:36,110
Ssik, kiss.

139
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:38,820
Ym...my...Ssa.

140
00:18:39,990 --> 00:18:42,620
Kiss my ass.

141
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:47,790
-I'm not playing this game! -Say it, it's serious.

142
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,370
It's very serious.

143
00:18:55,550 --> 00:18:57,630
Marry me.

144
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:01,470
I'm not gonna marry you. You're a fiend.

145
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,050
Uoy-evol-l-tub.

146
00:19:05,930 --> 00:19:07,560
Tub.

147
00:19:07,720 --> 00:19:09,560
But I...

148
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,350
love....

149
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:16,020
But I love you?

150
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:26,160
Tihs-ym-tae. WO What?

151
00:19:26,370 --> 00:19:28,950
Tihs-ym-tae.

152
00:19:31,870 --> 00:19:33,540
-Eat. -Eat.

153
00:19:33,750 --> 00:19:36,750
-Ym, my. -My.

154
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,750
Tihs. Eat my shit.

155
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:41,510
You filthy fiend!

156
00:19:41,720 --> 00:19:44,590
-You filthy! -Shh....

157
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:51,230
My music.

158
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,900
They've started without me.

159
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:11,560
That was Mozart!

160
00:21:12,850 --> 00:21:17,980
That giggling, dirty creature I'd just seen crawling on the floor.

161
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:22,480
-I think that went well, don't you? -Indeed.

162
00:21:22,690 --> 00:21:26,200
The Viennese know good music, don't you think?

163
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:27,450
Certainly.

164
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:32,200
Your Grace.

165
00:21:33,540 --> 00:21:36,620
Ah, Mozart.

166
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:40,710
-Why? -Why what, sir?

167
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:44,880
Why do I have to be humiliated in front of my guests...

168
00:21:45,090 --> 00:21:47,380
by one of my own servants?

169
00:21:47,630 --> 00:21:51,180
The more license I allow you, the more you take.

170
00:21:51,390 --> 00:21:55,310
If His Grace is not satisfied, he can dismiss me.

171
00:21:55,980 --> 00:21:59,560
I wish you to return immediately to Salzburg.

172
00:21:59,730 --> 00:22:03,690
-Your father is waiting for you there Patiently. -No, Your Grace!

173
00:22:04,230 --> 00:22:09,240
I would prefer you dismissed me. It's obvious I don't satisfy.

174
00:22:09,410 --> 00:22:14,830
I have no intention of dismissing you. You will remain in my service...

175
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:17,710
and learn your place.

176
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:57,950
On the page it looked....Nothing!

177
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:02,250
The beginning simple, almost comic.

178
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:08,920
Just a pulse.Bassoons, basset horns...

179
00:23:09,130 --> 00:23:12,130
like a rusty squeezebox.

180
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:17,640
And then, suddenly...

181
00:23:17,810 --> 00:23:20,060
high above it...

182
00:23:21,770 --> 00:23:24,060
an oboe.

183
00:23:26,190 --> 00:23:29,490
A single note, hanging there, unwavering.

184
00:23:31,910 --> 00:23:36,700
Until...a clarinet took it over...

185
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:43,500
sweetened it into a phrase of such delight.

186
00:23:47,500 --> 00:23:51,800
This was no composition by a performing monkey.

187
00:23:54,220 --> 00:23:57,970
This was a music I had never heard.

188
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:04,730
Filled with such longing, such unfulfillable longing.

189
00:24:06,770 --> 00:24:10,150
It seemed to me I was hearing the voice of God.

190
00:24:10,360 --> 00:24:11,610
Excuse me.

191
00:24:13,110 --> 00:24:14,860
But why?

192
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:20,660
Why would God choose an obscene child to be his instrument?

193
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:23,370
It was not to be believed.

194
00:24:23,540 --> 00:24:28,210
This piece had to be an accident. It had to be.

195
00:24:32,380 --> 00:24:34,010
It better be.

196
00:24:35,050 --> 00:24:37,470
How good is he, this Mozart?

197
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:43,270
He's remarkable, Majesty. I heard an extraordinary opera of his last month.

198
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:46,900
-Idomeneo, King of Crete.  That?

199
00:24:47,690 --> 00:24:50,230
A tiresome piece. I heard it too.

200
00:24:50,900 --> 00:24:52,150
Tiresome?

201
00:24:53,070 --> 00:24:57,360
A young man trying to impress beyond his abilities.

202
00:24:57,570 --> 00:25:02,290
Too much spice. Too many notes.

203
00:25:02,910 --> 00:25:07,920
Majesty...it was the most promising work I've heard in years.

204
00:25:08,080 --> 00:25:11,750
Then, we should make some effort to acquire him.

205
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:16,300
We could use a good German composer in Vienna, surely?

206
00:25:16,550 --> 00:25:21,180
I'm sure he could be tempted with the right offer. Say...

207
00:25:22,020 --> 00:25:25,430
an opera in German for our National Theater.

208
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:26,850
Excellent, sire!

209
00:25:27,810 --> 00:25:30,860
But not German. I beg, Your Majesty.

210
00:25:31,070 --> 00:25:35,440
Italian is the proper language for opera.

211
00:25:35,610 --> 00:25:38,360
All educated people agree on that.

212
00:25:39,700 --> 00:25:44,910
Mm-hm. What do you think, chamberlain?

213
00:25:45,460 --> 00:25:49,790
In my opinion, it's time we had a piece in our own language.

214
00:25:50,380 --> 00:25:54,460
Plain German for plain people.

215
00:25:57,470 --> 00:25:59,970
Kapellmeister?

216
00:26:00,220 --> 00:26:05,270
Majesty...I must agree with Herr Direttore.

217
00:26:06,810 --> 00:26:15,900
German is...scusate...too brute for singing.

218
00:26:19,570 --> 00:26:24,660
Court composer...what do you think?

219
00:26:25,660 --> 00:26:29,790
I think it's an interesting notion to keep Mozart in Vienna.

220
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:36,010
It should infuriate the archbishop...if that is Your Majesty's intention.

221
00:26:36,170 --> 00:26:39,680
You are cattivo, court composer.

222
00:26:41,970 --> 00:26:46,930
I want to meet this young man. Arrange a pleasant welcome for him.

223
00:26:47,520 --> 00:26:50,190
Well, there it is!

224
00:27:14,460 --> 00:27:16,210
Grazie, signore.

225
00:27:23,220 --> 00:27:30,230
This is a beautiful wig for you. It looks so marvelous and I love it.

226
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:31,690
The other one.

227
00:27:33,730 --> 00:27:37,190
Here is the other one. I think you will love it.

228
00:27:44,410 --> 00:27:48,080
-How do you like it? -They're all so beautiful!

229
00:27:48,240 --> 00:27:51,040
Why don't I have three heads?

230
00:27:52,330 --> 00:27:55,960
This is funny! Three heads!

231
00:27:58,710 --> 00:28:01,670
Good morning.  Morning, Your Majesty.

232
00:28:04,760 --> 00:28:07,220
What do you have for me today?

233
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:11,560
-Your Majesty, Herr Mozart.  Yes, what about him?

234
00:28:11,770 --> 00:28:13,730
He's here.

235
00:28:16,060 --> 00:28:17,940
Well, there it is. Good!

236
00:28:18,110 --> 00:28:23,610
I hope you won't find it improper, but I've written a march in his honor.

237
00:28:23,860 --> 00:28:27,910
What a charming idea, court composer. May I see?

238
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:32,370
Just a....Just a trifle, of course.

239
00:28:34,710 --> 00:28:35,960
May I try it?

240
00:28:36,790 --> 00:28:38,290
Majesty!

241
00:28:40,130 --> 00:28:42,510
Let's have some fun.

242
00:28:57,020 --> 00:29:00,150
Delightful, court composer!

243
00:29:01,480 --> 00:29:04,110
May I play it when he comes in?

244
00:29:05,070 --> 00:29:10,660
-You do me too much honor. -Bring in Herr Mozart. But slowly.

245
00:29:10,910 --> 00:29:13,540
I need a minute to practice.

246
00:29:37,020 --> 00:29:38,350
Good, continue.

247
00:29:40,940 --> 00:29:43,070
G, Majesty.

248
00:29:46,030 --> 00:29:48,110
Excellent!

249
00:29:56,790 --> 00:29:59,540
Very good, Majesty.

250
00:30:01,590 --> 00:30:04,300
Tempo! Up.

251
00:30:04,510 --> 00:30:10,050
Lightly, then strongly! It's a march, Majesty. Again.

252
00:30:49,090 --> 00:30:51,090
Bravo, Majesty!

253
00:30:51,760 --> 00:30:57,020
Gentlemen, please. A little less enthusiasm, I beg you.

254
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:01,770
-Mozart. -Majesty.

255
00:31:02,020 --> 00:31:05,730
No, please. It's not a holy relic.

256
00:31:08,610 --> 00:31:12,450
You know, we have met before. In this very room.

257
00:31:12,660 --> 00:31:17,580
You don't recall. You were only 6. He was giving a delightful concert!

258
00:31:18,250 --> 00:31:20,870
As he got off the stool, he fell.

259
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:24,960
My sister Antoinette helped him up. Know what he did?

260
00:31:25,170 --> 00:31:30,090
He jumped into her arms and said, "Will you marry me? Yes or no?"

261
00:31:33,970 --> 00:31:37,810
You know all these gentlemen. The Baron Van Swieten.

262
00:31:37,970 --> 00:31:41,770
-I'm a great admirer of yours. -Thank you.

263
00:31:41,980 --> 00:31:45,440
Kapellmeister Bonno. Signore.

264
00:31:45,650 --> 00:31:46,900
My pleasure.

265
00:31:47,110 --> 00:31:50,740
The Director of Opera, Count Orsini-Rosenberg.

266
00:31:50,950 --> 00:31:54,160
Sir, yes. The honor is mine, absolutely!

267
00:31:55,700 --> 00:32:01,750
Here is our illustrious court composer...Maestro Salieri.

268
00:32:03,250 --> 00:32:06,590
At last, such immense joy!

269
00:32:08,300 --> 00:32:10,340
I know your work well.

270
00:32:10,590 --> 00:32:15,180
You know, I composed some variations on a melody of yours.

271
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:19,930
-Really? Which one? -"Mio Caro Adone." I'm flattered.

272
00:32:20,140 --> 00:32:23,270
A funny tune, but it yielded good things.

273
00:32:23,480 --> 00:32:26,360
And now he has returned the compliment.

274
00:32:26,520 --> 00:32:30,150
Herr Salieri composed this little march for you.

275
00:32:30,360 --> 00:32:32,030
Really?

276
00:32:32,240 --> 00:32:34,150
Grazie, signore.

277
00:32:34,360 --> 00:32:35,860
Well, there it is.

278
00:32:36,030 --> 00:32:41,370
Down to business. We're going to commission an opera from you.

279
00:32:41,620 --> 00:32:43,370
What do you say?

280
00:32:43,540 --> 00:32:44,620
Majesty!

281
00:32:44,830 --> 00:32:48,210
Did we vote in the end for German or Italian?

282
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:54,130
Sire, if you remember, we did finally incline to Italian.

283
00:32:54,340 --> 00:32:56,390
Did we?

284
00:32:57,510 --> 00:33:01,390
I don't think it was really decided, Your Majesty.

285
00:33:02,890 --> 00:33:06,980
-German. Please let it be German. -Why so?

286
00:33:07,190 --> 00:33:11,230
Because I've already found the most wonderful libretto.

287
00:33:11,650 --> 00:33:13,690
Have I seen it?

288
00:33:14,400 --> 00:33:18,410
I don't think you have, Herr Direktor. It's quite new.

289
00:33:18,660 --> 00:33:23,040
-I'll show it to you immediately of course.

290
00:33:23,250 --> 00:33:24,580
Well...

291
00:33:25,160 --> 00:33:29,170
tell us about it. Tell us the story.

292
00:33:31,670 --> 00:33:35,380
Well, it's quite amusing, Majesty.

293
00:33:35,590 --> 00:33:40,300
It's set The whole thing is set in a....

294
00:33:45,810 --> 00:33:48,440
Yes? Where?

295
00:33:48,600 --> 00:33:52,610
In a harem, Majesty. In a seraglio.

296
00:33:52,860 --> 00:33:56,240
-You mean in Turkey? -Yes, exactly.

297
00:33:57,360 --> 00:34:01,740
Then why especially does it have to be in German?

298
00:34:02,450 --> 00:34:07,540
It doesn't, especially. It could be in Turkish if you really want.

299
00:34:08,120 --> 00:34:12,750
No, my dear fellow, the language is not finally the point.

300
00:34:12,960 --> 00:34:18,550
Do you really think that subject is appropriate for a national theater?

301
00:34:18,760 --> 00:34:21,640
Why not? It's charming.

302
00:34:22,140 --> 00:34:28,140
I mean, I won't actually show concubines exposing their....

303
00:34:28,850 --> 00:34:32,310
It's not indecent. It's highly moral, Majesty.

304
00:34:32,480 --> 00:34:35,320
It's full of proper German virtues.

305
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:39,860
Excuse me, Majesty, but what do you think these could be?

306
00:34:40,070 --> 00:34:42,990
Being a foreigner, I'd love to learn.

307
00:34:43,490 --> 00:34:49,500
Well, tell him, Mozart. Name us a German virtue.

308
00:34:49,750 --> 00:34:52,670
-Love, sire. -Oh, love!

309
00:34:52,920 --> 00:34:56,460
Of course, in Italy we know nothing about love.

310
00:35:00,300 --> 00:35:02,430
No, I don't think you do.

311
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:07,180
Watching Italian opera, all those male sopranos screeching...

312
00:35:07,430 --> 00:35:13,440
stupid, fat couples rolling their eyes about. That's not love. It's rubbish!

313
00:35:14,690 --> 00:35:18,190
Majesty, you choose the language.

314
00:35:18,400 --> 00:35:22,950
I'll set it to the finest music ever offered a monarch.

315
00:35:23,160 --> 00:35:26,790
Well, there it is. Let it be German.

316
00:35:29,040 --> 00:35:33,210
-This is yours. -Keep it. It's already here in my head.

317
00:35:33,460 --> 00:35:36,670
What? On one hearing only?

318
00:35:36,880 --> 00:35:40,130
I think so, sire. Yes.

319
00:35:43,510 --> 00:35:45,300
Show us.

320
00:36:15,080 --> 00:36:17,960
The rest is just the same, isn't it?

321
00:36:21,670 --> 00:36:24,590
That doesn't really work, does it?

322
00:36:26,890 --> 00:36:28,100
Did you try...?

323
00:36:30,220 --> 00:36:32,980
Shouldn't it be a bit more...?

324
00:36:33,350 --> 00:36:35,060
Or this?

325
00:36:35,270 --> 00:36:37,270
This. Yes.

326
00:36:41,780 --> 00:36:44,450
Better? What do you think?

327
00:37:36,120 --> 00:37:40,130
All I ever wanted was to sing to God.

328
00:37:40,420 --> 00:37:43,670
He gave me that longing...

329
00:37:44,340 --> 00:37:47,430
and then made me mute. Why?

330
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:50,760
Tell me that.

331
00:37:51,810 --> 00:37:55,640
If he didn't want me to praise him with music...

332
00:37:55,850 --> 00:37:58,650
why implant the desire...

333
00:37:58,980 --> 00:38:01,860
like a lust in my body?

334
00:38:02,360 --> 00:38:04,820
And then deny me the talent?

335
00:38:08,660 --> 00:38:11,780
Madame Cavalieri is here for her lesson, sir.

336
00:38:16,120 --> 00:38:17,370
Well...?

337
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:21,790
How do you like it?

338
00:38:23,210 --> 00:38:24,630
It's Turkish.

339
00:38:24,840 --> 00:38:29,380
My hairdresser said everything this year's going to be Turkish.

340
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:31,390
Does he?

341
00:38:34,560 --> 00:38:37,730
What else did he tell you today?

342
00:38:39,900 --> 00:38:43,520
Come, come! Give me some gossip.

343
00:38:45,320 --> 00:38:48,900
Well, I heard you met Herr Mozart.

344
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:54,620
News travels fast in Vienna.

345
00:38:54,990 --> 00:38:59,410
And he's been commissioned to write an opera. Is it true?

346
00:39:00,210 --> 00:39:03,420
-Yes. -Is there a part in it for me?

347
00:39:03,630 --> 00:39:06,340
-No. -How do you know?

348
00:39:06,550 --> 00:39:10,220
-Do you know where it's set, my dear? -Where?

349
00:39:10,430 --> 00:39:12,260
In a harem.

350
00:39:13,180 --> 00:39:16,560
-What's that? -A brothel.

351
00:39:20,600 --> 00:39:22,150
Come.

352
00:39:23,150 --> 00:39:25,020
Let's begin.

353
00:39:25,610 --> 00:39:29,030
-What does he look like? -Mozart?

354
00:39:29,280 --> 00:39:31,950
-You might be disappointed. -Why?

355
00:39:32,780 --> 00:39:37,120
Looks and talent don't always go together, Katerina.

356
00:39:37,330 --> 00:39:40,120
Looks don't concern me, maestro.

357
00:39:40,330 --> 00:39:44,630
Only talent interests a woman of taste.

358
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:47,340
Shall we continue?

359
00:40:25,170 --> 00:40:27,040
There she was.

360
00:40:28,880 --> 00:40:33,300
I don't know where they met or how. There she stood!

361
00:40:33,510 --> 00:40:35,840
On stage, for all to see.

362
00:40:36,050 --> 00:40:40,100
Showing off like the greedy songbird she was.

363
00:41:13,050 --> 00:41:18,550
Ten minutes of ghastly scales. Arpeggios!

364
00:41:18,760 --> 00:41:22,890
Whizzing up and down like fireworks at a fairground.

365
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:37,070
Understand, I was in love with the girl.

366
00:41:37,990 --> 00:41:40,070
Or at least in lust.

367
00:41:41,240 --> 00:41:45,580
And I swear to you, I never laid a finger on her.

368
00:41:49,880 --> 00:41:55,260
All the same, I couldn't bear to think of anyone else touching her.

369
00:41:55,420 --> 00:41:58,380
Least of all, "the creature."

370
00:43:41,990 --> 00:43:46,700
Brava, madame! You are an ornament to our stage.

371
00:43:47,910 --> 00:43:49,200
Your Majesty.

372
00:43:52,710 --> 00:43:55,790
Well, Herr Mozart. A good effort.

373
00:43:56,050 --> 00:43:57,710
Well, decidedly that.

374
00:43:57,920 --> 00:44:01,630
An excellent effort! You have shown us something...

375
00:44:03,390 --> 00:44:06,550
-...quite new tonight. -It is new.

376
00:44:06,760 --> 00:44:09,390
-It is, isn't it, sire? -Yes, indeed.

377
00:44:09,560 --> 00:44:13,940
So then, you liked it? You really liked it, sire?

378
00:44:14,150 --> 00:44:17,150
Well, of course I did! It's very good!

379
00:44:17,400 --> 00:44:21,400
Of course, now and then, just now and then...

380
00:44:21,610 --> 00:44:24,240
it seemed a touch....

381
00:44:25,620 --> 00:44:27,530
What do you mean, sire?

382
00:44:27,740 --> 00:44:31,950
Well, I mean, occasionally, it seems to have....

383
00:44:32,750 --> 00:44:35,120
How shall one say...?

384
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:40,250
How shall one say, direktor?

385
00:44:40,460 --> 00:44:44,050
-Too many notes, Majesty? -Exactly. Very well put.

386
00:44:44,260 --> 00:44:48,430
-Too many notes. -I don't understand.

387
00:44:48,640 --> 00:44:53,180
There are just as many notes as I required, neither more nor less.

388
00:44:53,440 --> 00:44:56,100
My dear fellow, there are in fact...

389
00:44:56,270 --> 00:45:00,190
only so many notes the ear can hear in an evening.

390
00:45:01,940 --> 00:45:06,450
I think I'm right in saying that, aren't I, court composer?

391
00:45:07,450 --> 00:45:10,950
Yes. On the whole, yes, Majesty.

392
00:45:11,580 --> 00:45:13,120
This is absurd!

393
00:45:13,330 --> 00:45:17,630
Young man, don't take it too hard. Your work is ingenious.

394
00:45:17,790 --> 00:45:19,460
It's quality work.

395
00:45:19,670 --> 00:45:25,220
And there are simply too many notes. Just cut a few and it'll be perfect.

396
00:45:25,590 --> 00:45:27,720
Which few did you have in mind?

397
00:45:31,470 --> 00:45:34,230
Wolfgang, my dear!

398
00:45:35,890 --> 00:45:42,650
-Wolfgang! -Majesty, this is Frau Weber. She's my landlady.

399
00:45:45,150 --> 00:45:50,830
-Enchanted, madame. -Sire, such an honor!

400
00:45:54,330 --> 00:45:57,670
This is my dear daughter, Constanze.

401
00:45:57,880 --> 00:46:01,670
-She's the fiancée of Herr Mozart. -Really?

402
00:46:06,180 --> 00:46:09,340
How charming. Please.

403
00:46:25,570 --> 00:46:31,370
Well...when do you marry? -Well....

404
00:46:32,240 --> 00:46:36,040
We haven't exactly received my father's consent yet.

405
00:46:36,290 --> 00:46:40,250
Not entirely. Not altogether.

406
00:46:42,960 --> 00:46:47,670
-Excuse me, but how old are you? -26.

407
00:46:48,260 --> 00:46:52,680
My advice is for you to marry this charming young lady...

408
00:46:52,890 --> 00:46:56,180
-...and stay with us in Vienna. -You see?

409
00:46:56,390 --> 00:46:59,480
I told him that, but he won't listen to me.

410
00:46:59,730 --> 00:47:03,480
Your Majesty, you give such wonderful...

411
00:47:03,900 --> 00:47:08,400
such royal advice. May I...?

412
00:47:17,750 --> 00:47:20,580
Well, there it is.

413
00:47:21,710 --> 00:47:24,500
Wolfie, will you get some water?

414
00:47:27,090 --> 00:47:30,130
Will you get some water, please?

415
00:47:34,260 --> 00:47:36,760
Wolfie, get some water!

416
00:47:45,110 --> 00:47:47,980
Excuse me. Excuse me.

417
00:47:55,450 --> 00:47:57,450
Did you know?

418
00:47:58,660 --> 00:48:00,960
-What? -The marriage.

419
00:48:03,830 --> 00:48:06,170
What does it matter to you?

420
00:48:06,380 --> 00:48:11,260
Nothing. He can marry who he pleases, I don't give a damn.

421
00:48:13,340 --> 00:48:15,470
How was I?

422
00:48:16,890 --> 00:48:18,810
You were sublime.

423
00:48:19,270 --> 00:48:22,140
And what did you think of the music?

424
00:48:23,400 --> 00:48:25,650
Extremely clever.

425
00:48:26,650 --> 00:48:28,690
Katerina, I

426
00:48:28,900 --> 00:48:30,480
Excuse me.

427
00:48:31,320 --> 00:48:34,860
Is that woman still lying on the floor?

428
00:48:35,070 --> 00:48:40,490
-No, she's fine. -Oh, I'm so relieved.

429
00:48:41,330 --> 00:48:44,210
Dear Mozart, my sincere congratulations.

430
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:48,840
-Did you like it then? -How could I not?

431
00:48:49,340 --> 00:48:52,920
It's the best music in Vienna today, don't you agree?

432
00:48:53,180 --> 00:48:56,300
She must be dazzling in bed.

433
00:48:58,390 --> 00:49:02,020
I assume she's the virtuoso in that department.

434
00:49:02,180 --> 00:49:05,100
No other reason why you'd marry someone like that.

435
00:49:07,610 --> 00:49:09,070
Come in.

436
00:49:11,900 --> 00:49:15,700
Excuse me. Wolfie, Mom isn't feeling very well.

437
00:49:15,910 --> 00:49:17,570
-Can we go home? -Yes.

438
00:49:17,820 --> 00:49:21,040
No, no, no. You can't take him away now.

439
00:49:21,240 --> 00:49:24,040
This is his night.

440
00:49:24,210 --> 00:49:26,830
Won't you introduce us, Wolfgang?

441
00:49:27,040 --> 00:49:30,710
Excuse us, Fr?ulein. Good night, signore.

442
00:49:32,210 --> 00:49:37,390
At that moment I knew, beyond any doubt...

443
00:49:37,550 --> 00:49:39,640
he'd had her.

444
00:49:39,890 --> 00:49:43,390
The creature had had my darling girl.

445
00:49:51,070 --> 00:49:53,730
It was incomprehensible!

446
00:49:54,240 --> 00:49:56,900
What was God up to?

447
00:49:58,240 --> 00:50:01,410
Was it possible I was being tested?

448
00:50:02,450 --> 00:50:07,080
Was God expecting me to offer forgiveness...

449
00:50:07,290 --> 00:50:10,080
in the face of every offense?

450
00:50:10,290 --> 00:50:12,130
No matter how painful?

451
00:50:14,420 --> 00:50:16,420
It's very possible.

452
00:50:16,880 --> 00:50:19,090
But why him?

453
00:50:19,930 --> 00:50:25,310
Why choose Mozart to teach me lessons in humility?

454
00:50:26,020 --> 00:50:31,150
My heart was filling up...with such hatred for that little man.

455
00:50:32,940 --> 00:50:36,440
For the first time in my life, I began to know...

456
00:50:36,610 --> 00:50:41,120
really...violent thoughts.

457
00:50:42,280 --> 00:50:47,410
Every day, sometimes for hours, I would pray.

458
00:50:48,670 --> 00:50:50,210
Lord...

459
00:50:51,420 --> 00:50:52,960
please...

460
00:50:54,050 --> 00:50:55,840
send him away...

461
00:50:56,050 --> 00:50:58,800
back to Salzburg.

462
00:51:00,640 --> 00:51:02,970
For his sake...

463
00:51:03,720 --> 00:51:06,220
as well as mine.

464
00:51:08,140 --> 00:51:12,230
-No! I won't have him back. -But, Your Grace

465
00:51:12,480 --> 00:51:17,820
Your son is an unprincipled, spoiled, conceited brat!

466
00:51:19,200 --> 00:51:24,160
Yes, sir...that is the truth.

467
00:51:25,660 --> 00:51:30,660
But don't blame him. The fault is mine, entirely.

468
00:51:30,830 --> 00:51:33,830
I was too indulgent with him.

469
00:51:34,460 --> 00:51:37,340
Please, Your Grace?

470
00:51:38,090 --> 00:51:40,340
Give him one more chance?

471
00:51:41,510 --> 00:51:44,010
You have leave to try.

472
00:51:44,220 --> 00:51:48,390
God bless, Your Grace! I thank Your Grace.

473
00:51:48,600 --> 00:51:50,560
I thank you!

474
00:51:54,270 --> 00:51:58,690
I write to you with urgent news. I'm coming to Vienna.

475
00:51:58,860 --> 00:52:02,740
Take no further steps towards marriage until we meet.

476
00:52:02,990 --> 00:52:07,080
As you honor the father who has devoted his life to yours...

477
00:52:07,290 --> 00:52:10,200
do as I bid, and await my coming.

478
00:52:23,720 --> 00:52:27,600
I now join you in the holy bonds of matrimony.

479
00:52:28,600 --> 00:52:31,390
Those whom God hath joined together...

480
00:52:31,600 --> 00:52:34,650
let no man put asunder.

481
00:52:48,240 --> 00:52:49,580
Beloved father:

482
00:52:49,790 --> 00:52:55,290
You say Vienna is the musicians' city. To conquer here is to conquer Europe.

483
00:52:55,540 --> 00:52:59,300
With my wife, I can do it. One day, when I'm wealthy...

484
00:52:59,550 --> 00:53:02,970
you'll live with us, and we'll be so happy.

485
00:53:13,440 --> 00:53:17,270
Good morning. This is my niece, Princess Elizabeth.

486
00:53:17,440 --> 00:53:18,690
Your Highness.

487
00:53:18,940 --> 00:53:22,280
She's asked me to recommend a music instructor.

488
00:53:22,440 --> 00:53:26,200
-I've come up with an excellent idea. -Your Majesty!

489
00:53:26,450 --> 00:53:29,330
It would be such a tremendous honor!

490
00:53:29,580 --> 00:53:33,830
I was thinking of Herr Mozart. What is your view?

491
00:53:35,330 --> 00:53:38,630
It's an interesting idea, Majesty, but....

492
00:53:39,880 --> 00:53:41,590
Yes?

493
00:53:41,960 --> 00:53:49,470
My concern is to protect you...from any hint of favoritism.

494
00:53:54,100 --> 00:53:55,600
Favoritism.

495
00:53:55,810 --> 00:53:58,400
-What is this? -What is what?

496
00:53:58,650 --> 00:54:04,490
Why must I submit samples of my work to a committee to teach a girl?

497
00:54:04,650 --> 00:54:07,400
Because His Majesty wishes it.

498
00:54:08,490 --> 00:54:10,870
Is the emperor angry with me?

499
00:54:11,120 --> 00:54:15,500
-Quite the contrary. -Then why not appoint me to the post?

500
00:54:15,710 --> 00:54:18,920
You are not the only composer in Vienna.

501
00:54:19,170 --> 00:54:22,420
No. But I'm the best.

502
00:54:23,340 --> 00:54:25,260
Mozart.

503
00:54:26,510 --> 00:54:30,180
A little modesty might suit you better.

504
00:54:37,270 --> 00:54:39,270
Who is on this committee?

505
00:54:39,690 --> 00:54:44,360
Kapellmeister Bonno, Count Orsini-Rosenberg and Salieri.

506
00:54:44,530 --> 00:54:49,070
Naturally, the Italians! Of course, always the Italians!

507
00:54:49,530 --> 00:54:52,070
They're all musical idiots!

508
00:54:53,030 --> 00:54:58,540
-And you want them to judge my music? -Young man...

509
00:54:58,710 --> 00:55:02,710
the issue is quite simple. If you want this position...

510
00:55:02,920 --> 00:55:07,380
you must submit your stuff, along with all your colleagues.

511
00:55:07,550 --> 00:55:09,430
-Must I? -Mm-hm.

512
00:55:10,930 --> 00:55:11,970
Well, I won't.

513
00:55:12,890 --> 00:55:15,390
How are we supposed to live?

514
00:55:16,980 --> 00:55:19,810
Do you want me to beg on the streets?

515
00:55:20,060 --> 00:55:22,060
Don't be stupid.

516
00:55:22,810 --> 00:55:25,900
-All they want to see is your work. -Shit.

517
00:55:26,070 --> 00:55:30,990
-What's wrong with that? -Shut up! Just shut up.

518
00:55:31,240 --> 00:55:35,490
One royal pupil, and all of Vienna will come flocking.

519
00:55:35,740 --> 00:55:37,910
They'll come anyway.

520
00:55:38,460 --> 00:55:42,080
-No, they won't. -They love me here.

521
00:55:42,290 --> 00:55:47,090
-I know how things work in this city. -You know everything, don't you?

522
00:56:15,620 --> 00:56:17,280
-Yes? -Excuse me, sir.

523
00:56:17,490 --> 00:56:20,450
-A lady insists on talking to you. -Who?

524
00:56:20,660 --> 00:56:24,250
She didn't say, but she says it's urgent.

525
00:56:26,460 --> 00:56:28,630
Excuse me, my dear.

526
00:56:36,760 --> 00:56:38,970
How can I help you?

527
00:56:43,980 --> 00:56:47,980
-Frau Mozart? -I've come on behalf of my husband.

528
00:56:48,190 --> 00:56:53,820
I brought samples of his work so he can be considered for the appointment.

529
00:56:55,490 --> 00:56:59,580
How charming, but why did he not come himself?

530
00:57:01,200 --> 00:57:04,160
Well, he's terribly busy, sir.

531
00:57:07,590 --> 00:57:09,000
I understand.

532
00:57:11,510 --> 00:57:14,680
I will look at them the moment I can.

533
00:57:14,880 --> 00:57:19,300
It will be an honor. Please give him my warmest regards.

534
00:57:19,510 --> 00:57:23,850
Would it be too much trouble to ask you to look at them now?

535
00:57:24,190 --> 00:57:30,570
-While I wait. -I'm afraid I'm not at leisure...this precise moment.

536
00:57:30,820 --> 00:57:34,700
Leave them with me. I assure you, they will be safe.

537
00:57:35,700 --> 00:57:38,740
I really cannot do that, sir.

538
00:57:39,410 --> 00:57:42,870
You see, he doesn't know I'm here.

539
00:57:44,580 --> 00:57:47,040
Then he didn't send you?

540
00:57:47,250 --> 00:57:50,920
No, sir. This was my own idea.

541
00:57:53,340 --> 00:57:57,050
-I see. -Sir, we're desperate.

542
00:57:57,970 --> 00:58:01,050
We really need this job.

543
00:58:01,260 --> 00:58:04,890
My husband spends far more than he can ever earn.

544
00:58:05,060 --> 00:58:09,400
I don't mean that he's lazy, because he works all day long.

545
00:58:09,610 --> 00:58:14,070
It's just that he's not practical.

546
00:58:14,400 --> 00:58:18,570
Money simply slips through his fingers. It's ridiculous.

547
00:58:21,660 --> 00:58:24,410
Let me offer you some refreshment.

548
00:58:24,620 --> 00:58:26,960
Do you know what these are?

549
00:58:28,630 --> 00:58:32,090
Capezzoli di Venere! Nipples of Venus.

550
00:58:33,090 --> 00:58:38,090
They're Roman chestnuts in brandied sugar. Try one. Go on!

551
00:58:38,260 --> 00:58:40,800
They're quite surprising.

552
00:58:45,640 --> 00:58:47,600
They're wonderful!

553
00:58:49,600 --> 00:58:52,610
Thank you very much, Your Excellency.

554
00:58:52,770 --> 00:58:55,440
Don't keep calling me that.

555
00:58:56,280 --> 00:58:58,950
Keeps me at such a distance.

556
00:58:59,660 --> 00:59:02,780
I wasn't born a court composer, you know.

557
00:59:02,990 --> 00:59:05,120
I'm from a small town.

558
00:59:05,330 --> 00:59:07,450
Just like your husband.

559
00:59:09,960 --> 00:59:12,790
Are you sure you can't...

560
00:59:13,000 --> 00:59:16,670
leave this and come back again?

561
00:59:17,840 --> 00:59:20,800
It's very tempting, sir.

562
00:59:20,970 --> 00:59:24,300
But it's impossible, I'm afraid.

563
00:59:24,680 --> 00:59:27,850
He'd be frantic if he knew they were missing.

564
00:59:28,060 --> 00:59:30,940
You see, they're all originals.

565
00:59:31,810 --> 00:59:35,190
-Originals? -Yes, sir. He doesn't make copies.

566
00:59:46,950 --> 00:59:50,370
These...are originals?

567
01:00:26,870 --> 01:00:28,370
Astounding!

568
01:00:28,870 --> 01:00:32,370
It was actually. It was beyond belief.

569
01:00:33,120 --> 01:00:35,750
These were first and only...

570
01:00:36,380 --> 01:00:38,550
drafts of music.

571
01:00:39,800 --> 01:00:45,390
But they showed no corrections of any kind. Not one.

572
01:00:48,220 --> 01:00:51,560
He had simply written down music...

573
01:00:51,730 --> 01:00:54,730
already finished in his head.

574
01:00:55,020 --> 01:01:00,530
Page after page of it. As if he were just taking dictation.

575
01:01:07,240 --> 01:01:13,460
And music...finished as no music is ever finished.

576
01:01:16,580 --> 01:01:22,300
Displace one note...and there would be diminishment.

577
01:01:23,550 --> 01:01:27,760
Displace one phrase, and the structure would fall.

578
01:01:31,430 --> 01:01:33,980
It was clear to me...

579
01:01:34,560 --> 01:01:38,560
that sound I had heard in the archbishop's palace...

580
01:01:38,770 --> 01:01:41,690
had been no accident.

581
01:01:42,570 --> 01:01:47,570
Here again was the very voice of God.

582
01:01:51,700 --> 01:01:54,450
I was staring through the cage...

583
01:01:54,620 --> 01:01:58,290
of those meticulous ink strokes...

584
01:01:59,630 --> 01:02:03,630
at an absolute beauty.

585
01:02:19,020 --> 01:02:21,480
Is it not good?

586
01:02:26,150 --> 01:02:27,650
It is miraculous.

587
01:02:31,660 --> 01:02:36,040
Yes, he's very proud of his work.

588
01:02:38,370 --> 01:02:40,670
So you will help us?

589
01:02:42,710 --> 01:02:45,760
I dine with the emperor tomorrow evening.

590
01:02:46,010 --> 01:02:49,430
One word from me and the post is his.

591
01:02:49,680 --> 01:02:52,430
Thank you, Your Excellency! Thank you!

592
01:02:52,930 --> 01:02:55,220
Come back tonight.

593
01:02:56,560 --> 01:02:58,940
-Tonight? -Alone.

594
01:03:01,520 --> 01:03:02,770
What for?

595
01:03:04,400 --> 01:03:08,200
Some service deserves service in return.

596
01:03:09,860 --> 01:03:11,530
No?

597
01:03:12,950 --> 01:03:16,750
-What do you mean? -Isn't it obvious?

598
01:03:17,580 --> 01:03:20,870
It's a post all Vienna seeks.

599
01:03:21,080 --> 01:03:25,050
If you wish it for your husband, come tonight.

600
01:03:25,550 --> 01:03:28,260
I'm a married woman, sir.

601
01:03:28,470 --> 01:03:30,180
Then don't.

602
01:03:30,720 --> 01:03:32,680
It's up to you.

603
01:03:33,220 --> 01:03:36,470
And not to be vague, that is the price.

604
01:03:48,610 --> 01:03:51,950
There is no God of mercy, Father.

605
01:03:54,240 --> 01:03:57,200
Just a God of torture.

606
01:04:03,330 --> 01:04:05,420
Evening came.

607
01:04:06,460 --> 01:04:11,130
I sat there, not knowing whether she would return or not.

608
01:04:11,760 --> 01:04:16,640
I prayed as I had never prayed before.

609
01:04:17,640 --> 01:04:19,930
Dear God...

610
01:04:20,100 --> 01:04:22,480
enter me now.

611
01:04:22,730 --> 01:04:27,320
Fill me with one piece of true music.

612
01:04:27,530 --> 01:04:32,820
One piece with your breath in it, so I know that you love me.

613
01:04:33,110 --> 01:04:39,040
Show me one sign of your favor, and I will show mine to Mozart.

614
01:04:39,790 --> 01:04:43,830
I will get him the royal position.

615
01:04:44,170 --> 01:04:46,000
Enter me.

616
01:04:46,250 --> 01:04:48,130
Please.

617
01:04:49,510 --> 01:04:51,670
Please!

618
01:04:58,350 --> 01:04:59,640
Yes?

619
01:05:03,850 --> 01:05:06,650
That lady is back, sir.

620
01:05:11,030 --> 01:05:12,320
Show her in.

621
01:05:49,110 --> 01:05:51,020
I'm here.

622
01:05:54,610 --> 01:05:58,030
My husband has gone to a concert.

623
01:05:58,700 --> 01:06:01,700
He didn't think I would enjoy it.

624
01:06:12,420 --> 01:06:15,220
Well, where shall we go?

625
01:06:16,430 --> 01:06:19,220
Should we stay here?

626
01:06:25,890 --> 01:06:28,770
Do you still want to look at these?

627
01:06:31,570 --> 01:06:34,860
Or don't we need to bother anymore?

628
01:06:36,740 --> 01:06:39,610
Suppose we don't, really.

629
01:07:36,630 --> 01:07:38,720
Show this woman out.

630
01:08:00,200 --> 01:08:01,820
Stanzi.

631
01:08:03,450 --> 01:08:05,330
Stanzi.

632
01:08:11,080 --> 01:08:13,040
What is it?

633
01:08:13,880 --> 01:08:17,460
What's the matter? Tell me.

634
01:08:20,720 --> 01:08:22,680
Tell me.

635
01:08:28,060 --> 01:08:30,350
I love you.

636
01:08:31,190 --> 01:08:33,520
I love you.

637
01:08:34,730 --> 01:08:38,480
From now on, we are enemies.

638
01:08:38,690 --> 01:08:40,280
You and I.

639
01:08:40,530 --> 01:08:43,360
Because you choose for your instrument...

640
01:08:43,530 --> 01:08:48,370
a boastful, lustful, smutty, infantile boy...

641
01:08:48,620 --> 01:08:54,540
and give me for reward only the ability to recognize the incarnation.

642
01:08:55,210 --> 01:08:58,130
Because you are unjust...

643
01:08:58,550 --> 01:09:00,210
unfair...

644
01:09:01,220 --> 01:09:03,380
unkind...

645
01:09:03,590 --> 01:09:07,320
I will block you. I swear it.

646
01:09:08,220 --> 01:09:11,720
I will hinder and harm your creature on earth...

647
01:09:11,890 --> 01:09:14,230
as far as I am able.

648
01:09:14,600 --> 01:09:18,150
I don't like to talk against a fellow musician.

649
01:09:18,400 --> 01:09:19,900
Of course not.

650
01:09:20,070 --> 01:09:22,280
I have to tell you.

651
01:09:23,240 --> 01:09:28,450
Mozart is not entirely to be trusted alone with young ladies.

652
01:09:28,660 --> 01:09:30,580
Really?

653
01:09:30,740 --> 01:09:34,790
One of my own pupils, a very young singer...

654
01:09:35,040 --> 01:09:37,080
Maria Theresa Paradis...

655
01:09:37,250 --> 01:09:39,460
told me she was....

656
01:09:45,260 --> 01:09:47,550
Well, what?

657
01:09:48,180 --> 01:09:50,640
Molested, Majesty.

658
01:09:50,850 --> 01:09:54,140
Twice, in the course of the same lesson.

659
01:09:58,810 --> 01:10:03,190
There is a Herr Mozart waiting for you in the salon.

660
01:10:07,110 --> 01:10:10,120
-Whom did they choose? -Herr Zummer.

661
01:10:10,490 --> 01:10:12,580
Herr Zummer?

662
01:10:12,790 --> 01:10:16,460
But the man's a fool! He's a total mediocrity.

663
01:10:16,620 --> 01:10:21,500
No, no. He has yet to achieve mediocrity.

664
01:10:23,510 --> 01:10:27,630
I can't lose this post. I simply can't.

665
01:10:28,970 --> 01:10:30,970
Excellency, please.

666
01:10:31,140 --> 01:10:35,140
Let's go to the palace. You can talk to the emperor...

667
01:10:35,350 --> 01:10:39,520
and tell him that Herr Zummer is an awful choice.

668
01:10:39,730 --> 01:10:42,820
He could do musical harm to the princess.

669
01:10:42,980 --> 01:10:48,400
Between us, no one in the world could do musical harm to the princess.

670
01:10:52,490 --> 01:10:56,120
Look...I must have pupils.

671
01:10:56,330 --> 01:10:59,170
Without pupils, I can't manage.

672
01:10:59,670 --> 01:11:03,130
You don't mean you're living in poverty?

673
01:11:03,340 --> 01:11:06,670
No, but I'm broke.

674
01:11:06,840 --> 01:11:08,930
Well, how is this possible?

675
01:11:09,180 --> 01:11:12,180
I hear your concerts are quite successful.

676
01:11:12,510 --> 01:11:15,520
They're stupendously successful.

677
01:11:15,720 --> 01:11:19,520
You can't get a seat. But no one will hire me.

678
01:11:19,690 --> 01:11:26,440
They want to hear me play, but they won't let me teach their daughters, as if I was a fiend.

679
01:11:31,700 --> 01:11:33,700
Seriously...

680
01:11:33,910 --> 01:11:37,290
is there any chance you could manage a loan?

681
01:11:38,040 --> 01:11:42,210
Only for six months. Eight, at the most.

682
01:11:42,420 --> 01:11:46,710
You expect your fortunes to change in six or eight months?

683
01:11:46,920 --> 01:11:49,590
As a matter of fact, I do.

684
01:11:50,430 --> 01:11:55,720
I am working on something that will explode like a bomb all over Europe.

685
01:11:55,930 --> 01:12:01,230
I'll be the richest man in Vienna. I'll pay you back double. Anything.

686
01:12:01,440 --> 01:12:03,440
You name the terms.

687
01:12:03,690 --> 01:12:05,770
Well, how exciting.

688
01:12:06,110 --> 01:12:08,400
Tell me more.

689
01:12:10,110 --> 01:12:14,070
-It's a bit of a secret. -Come, come. I'm interested.

690
01:12:14,280 --> 01:12:16,910
This is delicious. What is it?

691
01:12:17,750 --> 01:12:20,710
It's cream cheese mixed with sugar...

692
01:12:20,910 --> 01:12:25,250
suffused with rum. Crema Mascarpone Speciale.

693
01:12:25,460 --> 01:12:27,090
Italian.

694
01:12:27,250 --> 01:12:31,760
Forgive me. We all have patriotic feelings of some kind.

695
01:12:32,010 --> 01:12:33,800
Two thou

696
01:12:34,010 --> 01:12:37,510
Two hundred florins. That's all I need.

697
01:12:39,430 --> 01:12:41,100
A hundred.

698
01:12:43,310 --> 01:12:44,770
Fifty.

699
01:12:45,770 --> 01:12:49,030
What exactly are you working on?

700
01:12:51,490 --> 01:12:54,860
Really, I can't say.

701
01:12:55,620 --> 01:13:01,790
I don't think you should become known in Vienna as a debtor, Mozart.

702
01:13:08,500 --> 01:13:10,380
However...

703
01:13:10,630 --> 01:13:14,800
I know a distinguished gentleman I can recommend, and...

704
01:13:14,970 --> 01:13:16,300
he has a daughter.

705
01:13:21,140 --> 01:13:23,810
Quiet! Quiet!

706
01:13:23,980 --> 01:13:26,060
Herr Mozart.

707
01:13:26,310 --> 01:13:29,980
Welcome. Pay no attention, they're impossible.

708
01:13:30,190 --> 01:13:33,490
I treat them just like my own children.

709
01:13:34,280 --> 01:13:37,280
Which of them do you wish me to teach?

710
01:13:40,660 --> 01:13:42,830
That's funny.

711
01:13:43,500 --> 01:13:46,330
You're a funny fellow.

712
01:13:46,500 --> 01:13:51,000
This is the instrument. I hope it's to your satisfaction.

713
01:13:51,210 --> 01:13:54,300
MICHAEL: Of course it'll be to his satisfaction.

714
01:13:54,510 --> 01:13:58,340
Come, we're going to listen to some music. Come!

715
01:13:59,010 --> 01:14:01,010
Good boy.

716
01:14:06,690 --> 01:14:08,190
Now.

717
01:14:08,360 --> 01:14:12,570
Please play me something, just to give me an idea.

718
01:14:13,530 --> 01:14:15,740
Anything will do.

719
01:14:17,070 --> 01:14:18,360
Just go ahead.

720
01:14:18,570 --> 01:14:21,530
Just as if we weren't here.

721
01:14:22,830 --> 01:14:27,750
Part of music, getting used to an audience. Right, Herr Mozart?

722
01:14:27,960 --> 01:14:31,540
Perhaps it would be better if we were left alone.

723
01:14:31,710 --> 01:14:33,710
We're both a little shy.

724
01:14:33,920 --> 01:14:35,210
Play.

725
01:14:35,380 --> 01:14:38,590
-I said play! -Michael, please.

726
01:14:38,840 --> 01:14:43,140
Perhaps if I play first, it might encourage the Fr?ulein.

727
01:14:43,600 --> 01:14:45,930
Why don't you let me try?

728
01:14:55,740 --> 01:14:59,610
Stop it! Stop! He always howls when he hears music.

729
01:14:59,870 --> 01:15:02,660
We've got to break him of that habit.

730
01:15:02,910 --> 01:15:06,370
We've got to break them of their habit!

731
01:15:06,580 --> 01:15:07,870
Play. Please.

732
01:15:08,290 --> 01:15:12,590
Herr Mozart, play. Please, I beg you.

733
01:15:19,930 --> 01:15:22,090
That's it. That's it.

734
01:15:25,100 --> 01:15:27,390
Keep playing!

735
01:15:33,320 --> 01:15:36,320
Keep playing! That's it!

736
01:15:55,800 --> 01:15:59,010
Mozart, that's wonderful! Wonderful!

737
01:15:59,220 --> 01:16:04,140
Next time you wish me to instruct another of your dogs, let me know.

738
01:16:04,300 --> 01:16:07,970
Goodbye, Fr?ulein. Goodbye, madam. Goodbye, sir.

739
01:17:05,200 --> 01:17:07,070
Papa?

740
01:17:10,870 --> 01:17:12,580
Papa!

741
01:17:16,630 --> 01:17:18,540
Why are you here?

742
01:17:18,710 --> 01:17:20,420
Am I not welcome?

743
01:17:20,710 --> 01:17:25,260
Of course, welcome. Papa, welcome! Welcome!

744
01:17:46,820 --> 01:17:50,580
You're very thin. Doesn't your wife feed you?

745
01:17:50,790 --> 01:17:55,120
Of course she feeds me. She stuffs me like a goose all day!

746
01:17:56,250 --> 01:17:59,920
Is she not here?  No, she had to help her mother.

747
01:18:00,130 --> 01:18:01,920
She's like that.

748
01:18:02,130 --> 01:18:05,170
Her mother's a very sweet woman, you'll

749
01:18:13,100 --> 01:18:16,270
I didn't know you were home.

750
01:18:17,060 --> 01:18:19,610
Stanzi, this is my father.

751
01:18:21,860 --> 01:18:25,320
We'll wait. We'll wait.

752
01:18:27,280 --> 01:18:30,450
Why don't you get up now, my darling?

753
01:18:36,580 --> 01:18:41,170
She's very tired, poor creature. You know me. I'm such a pig.

754
01:18:41,380 --> 01:18:44,300
It's not easy cleaning up after me.

755
01:18:45,130 --> 01:18:47,170
Don't you have a maid?

756
01:18:47,380 --> 01:18:51,140
Oh. No. We could if we wanted...

757
01:18:51,300 --> 01:18:55,640
but Stanzi insists on doing everything herself.

758
01:18:56,140 --> 01:19:01,650
How is your...financial situation?

759
01:19:01,900 --> 01:19:03,980
Couldn't be better.

760
01:19:04,820 --> 01:19:06,900
That's not what I hear.

761
01:19:07,150 --> 01:19:10,110
What do you mean? It's wonderful.

762
01:19:10,320 --> 01:19:14,660
Really, it's marvelous! People love me here.

763
01:19:15,200 --> 01:19:18,000
They say you have debts.

764
01:19:18,330 --> 01:19:19,830
Who?

765
01:19:20,420 --> 01:19:22,380
Who says that?

766
01:19:22,630 --> 01:19:24,920
That's a malicious lie!

767
01:19:25,170 --> 01:19:27,340
Do you have pupils?

768
01:19:27,920 --> 01:19:30,930
I don't want pupils!

769
01:19:31,180 --> 01:19:33,640
They get in the way.

770
01:19:34,850 --> 01:19:37,680
I have to have time for composition.

771
01:19:38,020 --> 01:19:40,940
Composition doesn't pay. You know that.

772
01:19:41,150 --> 01:19:43,110
That one will.

773
01:19:43,730 --> 01:19:45,610
What's that?

774
01:19:47,030 --> 01:19:48,780
It's a secret.

775
01:19:48,990 --> 01:19:51,990
Secret? You don't have secrets from me.

776
01:19:52,200 --> 01:19:53,240
No.

777
01:19:53,450 --> 01:19:58,870
No! Please! I don't want you to see it. I don't want anyone to see it.

778
01:19:59,040 --> 01:20:01,120
You'll be so proud of me.

779
01:20:01,330 --> 01:20:05,840
It'll be the best thing I've ever done. The best thing anyone

780
01:20:08,170 --> 01:20:09,510
There she is!

781
01:20:09,720 --> 01:20:13,890
Look at her! Isn't she beautiful? Now, Papa, confess it.

782
01:20:14,050 --> 01:20:18,770
-Could you want a prettier daughter? -Stop it, Wolfie!

783
01:20:19,560 --> 01:20:21,690
I look dreadful.

784
01:20:22,850 --> 01:20:24,400
Are you...

785
01:20:24,560 --> 01:20:26,770
expecting?

786
01:20:26,980 --> 01:20:30,900
-Yes, I am. -Isn't it marvelous? We're delighted.

787
01:20:31,910 --> 01:20:36,330
-May I offer you some tea? -Who wants tea? Let's go out!

788
01:20:36,540 --> 01:20:40,330
This calls for a feast. You don't want tea, do you, Papa?

789
01:20:40,540 --> 01:20:44,830
I know! Let's go dancing. Papa loves parties, don't you?

790
01:20:45,040 --> 01:20:48,340
How can you be so boring? Tea!

791
01:20:52,550 --> 01:20:54,510
Come on, Papa. Hurry!

792
01:20:54,720 --> 01:20:56,510
Here we go. Good day.

793
01:21:39,140 --> 01:21:40,720
Now!

794
01:21:46,350 --> 01:21:50,980
I name the penalty! I name the penalty!

795
01:21:51,780 --> 01:21:54,570
And the penalty is....

796
01:21:54,780 --> 01:21:58,870
-Give her a good one! -Show us your legs!

797
01:22:03,250 --> 01:22:05,500
Come on, come on!

798
01:22:18,140 --> 01:22:20,760
It's just a game, Papa.

799
01:22:33,530 --> 01:22:35,190
Thank you.

800
01:22:47,670 --> 01:22:49,210
Now!

801
01:22:59,800 --> 01:23:04,140
Herr Mozart, why don't you name your son's penalty?!

802
01:23:06,230 --> 01:23:09,350
Yes, Papa. Name it.

803
01:23:09,850 --> 01:23:14,150
Name it. I'll do anything you say. Anything.

804
01:23:15,530 --> 01:23:19,410
I want you to come back to Salzburg with me.

805
01:23:19,570 --> 01:23:23,160
The penalty must be performed in the room.

806
01:23:23,370 --> 01:23:25,240
I'm tired of this game.

807
01:23:25,700 --> 01:23:30,250
But my penalty! I've got to have a penalty!

808
01:23:34,840 --> 01:23:37,010
I name a penalty!

809
01:23:39,880 --> 01:23:41,260
The penalty is...

810
01:23:41,760 --> 01:23:44,010
you shall play our tune...

811
01:23:44,220 --> 01:23:48,850
in the manner of Johann Sebastian Bach!

812
01:24:15,750 --> 01:24:18,630
-Turn him over! -Over?!

813
01:24:20,630 --> 01:24:23,390
Now you play it backwards!

814
01:24:50,790 --> 01:24:55,290
-Another one! Another one! -Play it like Gluck!

815
01:24:55,500 --> 01:24:58,250
-Boring. Another! -Handel!

816
01:24:58,460 --> 01:25:00,920
I don't like him! Another one!

817
01:25:01,420 --> 01:25:03,630
Play Salieri.

818
01:25:04,340 --> 01:25:07,970
Now, that is a challenge! That is a challenge.

819
01:25:08,430 --> 01:25:11,180
Please! Please!

820
01:25:45,720 --> 01:25:48,600
Go on. Mock me. Laugh!

821
01:25:53,560 --> 01:25:56,400
That was not Mozart laughing, Father.

822
01:25:56,650 --> 01:25:58,230
That was God.

823
01:25:58,480 --> 01:26:03,150
That was God laughing at me through that obscene giggle.

824
01:26:06,410 --> 01:26:08,910
Go on, signore. Laugh.

825
01:26:09,120 --> 01:26:13,330
Show my mediocrity for all to see.

826
01:26:14,710 --> 01:26:17,580
One day I will laugh at you.

827
01:26:20,670 --> 01:26:23,590
Before I leave this earth...

828
01:26:23,760 --> 01:26:26,590
I will laugh at you.

829
01:26:48,360 --> 01:26:50,950
-Wolfie? -What?

830
01:26:52,080 --> 01:26:54,950
There's a young girl here to see you.

831
01:26:55,210 --> 01:26:56,710
What does she want?

832
01:26:56,920 --> 01:27:01,460
She won't talk to me. She says she has to speak to you.

833
01:27:02,880 --> 01:27:04,380
Damn.

834
01:27:09,300 --> 01:27:10,590
Yes?

835
01:27:12,470 --> 01:27:15,390
-Are you Herr Mozart? -That's right.

836
01:27:17,190 --> 01:27:20,980
My name is Lorl, sir. I'm a maidservant.

837
01:27:21,230 --> 01:27:25,190
I was asked to come here and offer my services to you.

838
01:27:25,400 --> 01:27:32,740
They'll be paid for by an admirer of yours who wishes to remain...anonymous.

839
01:27:33,410 --> 01:27:36,290
Is this your idea, Papa?

840
01:27:37,250 --> 01:27:38,500
Mine?

841
01:27:38,710 --> 01:27:43,000
-Are you playing a trick on me? -I've never seen this girl.

842
01:27:43,960 --> 01:27:47,590
-Is this some kind of joke? -Not at all, sir.

843
01:27:47,800 --> 01:27:50,180
Young woman, this won't do.

844
01:27:50,340 --> 01:27:54,810
My son can't accept such an offer, no matter how generous...

845
01:27:55,010 --> 01:27:59,520
-...unless he knows who's behind it. -I can't tell you that, sir.

846
01:27:59,730 --> 01:28:02,940
This is ridiculous! -What is ridiculous?

847
01:28:03,150 --> 01:28:05,860
Wolfie has many admirers in Vienna.

848
01:28:06,030 --> 01:28:08,820
People send us gifts all the time.

849
01:28:09,030 --> 01:28:12,030
You cannot accept her without references.

850
01:28:12,280 --> 01:28:15,240
Well, this is none of your business.

851
01:28:15,450 --> 01:28:19,200
-Whoever sent you is going to pay? -That's right.

852
01:28:19,370 --> 01:28:23,790
Splendid! Now we're going to let a stranger into our house.

853
01:28:24,000 --> 01:28:27,170
Who is we? Who is letting who?

854
01:28:30,760 --> 01:28:34,680
-Could you please wait outside? -Yes, ma'am.

855
01:28:34,890 --> 01:28:36,220
Look, old man!

856
01:28:36,390 --> 01:28:40,890
We spend a fortune on you, and all you can do is criticize.

857
01:28:41,140 --> 01:28:42,390
-And now -Stanzi!

858
01:28:42,560 --> 01:28:47,070
No! It's right that he should hear! I'm sick to death of it.

859
01:28:47,320 --> 01:28:50,820
We can't do anything right for you, can we?

860
01:28:51,030 --> 01:28:54,870
You won't have to do anything for me ever again.

861
01:28:55,070 --> 01:28:56,740
I'm leaving.

862
01:28:56,910 --> 01:29:00,080
-No, Papa.  I won't stay and be a burden.

863
01:29:00,290 --> 01:29:02,210
No one calls you that.

864
01:29:02,420 --> 01:29:05,880
She does. She says I sleep all day.

865
01:29:06,090 --> 01:29:07,920
And so you do!

866
01:29:08,210 --> 01:29:11,340
The only time you come out is to eat.

867
01:29:12,590 --> 01:29:14,840
Well, what do you expect?

868
01:29:17,060 --> 01:29:21,890
Do you expect anyone to walk out into a mess like this every day?

869
01:29:22,100 --> 01:29:26,900
-Now I'm a bad housekeeper! -So you are. It's a pigsty.

870
01:29:27,110 --> 01:29:29,320
When can you start?

871
01:29:29,530 --> 01:29:31,740
-Right away, ma'am.  Good.

872
01:29:58,890 --> 01:30:01,640
They're out every night, sir.

873
01:30:03,980 --> 01:30:05,980
Thank you, sir.

874
01:30:06,600 --> 01:30:09,770
Do any pupils come to the house?

875
01:30:11,820 --> 01:30:13,860
Not that I've seen.

876
01:30:14,070 --> 01:30:16,860
Then how does he pay for all this?

877
01:30:17,870 --> 01:30:20,160
Does he work at all?

878
01:30:20,410 --> 01:30:26,330
Yes, sir. All day long. He never leaves the house till evening.

879
01:30:26,500 --> 01:30:29,580
He just sits there, writing and writing.

880
01:30:29,790 --> 01:30:31,590
Really?

881
01:30:32,920 --> 01:30:35,170
What is it he's writing?

882
01:30:38,180 --> 01:30:40,760
I wouldn't know that, sir.

883
01:30:40,970 --> 01:30:42,760
Of course not.

884
01:30:42,970 --> 01:30:44,980
You're a good girl.

885
01:30:45,180 --> 01:30:47,600
You're very kind to do this.

886
01:30:47,810 --> 01:30:53,020
The next time you're sure they'll be out of the house, let me know.

887
01:30:59,320 --> 01:31:01,870
Thank you, sir.

888
01:32:41,130 --> 01:32:44,510
I think I found out about the money, sir.

889
01:32:45,300 --> 01:32:47,810
Yes? What?

890
01:32:48,060 --> 01:32:53,060
He kept seven snuffboxes in here. I could swear they were all gold.

891
01:32:53,520 --> 01:32:55,560
And now look.

892
01:32:55,770 --> 01:32:57,900
There's only one left.

893
01:32:58,990 --> 01:33:01,400
Where does he work?

894
01:33:02,910 --> 01:33:05,160
In there, sir.

895
01:33:50,540 --> 01:33:54,000
Gentlemen, I've just heard some news...

896
01:33:54,370 --> 01:33:57,500
-that may interest you. -What?

897
01:33:57,710 --> 01:34:02,090
Mozart is writing a new opera. An Italian opera.

898
01:34:02,590 --> 01:34:04,720
Italian?

899
01:34:05,510 --> 01:34:09,720
That's not all. He has chosen for his subject, Figaro.

900
01:34:10,390 --> 01:34:13,180
The Marriage of Figaro.

901
01:34:13,390 --> 01:34:16,900
He's setting that play to music?

902
01:34:17,360 --> 01:34:18,610
Yes.

903
01:34:19,860 --> 01:34:23,320
What is this Marriage of Figaro?

904
01:34:23,530 --> 01:34:26,990
It's a French play, Kapellmeister.

905
01:34:27,200 --> 01:34:30,410
It has been banned by the emperor.

906
01:34:30,620 --> 01:34:32,660
You're absolutely sure?

907
01:34:36,250 --> 01:34:38,580
Herr Mozart.

908
01:34:39,540 --> 01:34:41,670
Gentlemen, sit down.

909
01:34:46,430 --> 01:34:48,130
Mozart.

910
01:34:49,390 --> 01:34:56,730
Are you aware that I have declared the French play Figaro...unsuitable for our theater?

911
01:34:57,900 --> 01:34:59,690
Yes, sire.

912
01:34:59,900 --> 01:35:05,070
Yet we hear you're making an opera from it. Is this true?

913
01:35:08,700 --> 01:35:10,910
Who told you this, Majesty?

914
01:35:11,120 --> 01:35:15,790
It is not your place to ask questions. Is it true?

915
01:35:15,960 --> 01:35:17,960
Yes, I....

916
01:35:18,420 --> 01:35:20,710
I admit it is.

917
01:35:22,800 --> 01:35:25,300
Would you tell me why?

918
01:35:27,380 --> 01:35:29,800
Majesty, it is only a comedy.

919
01:35:30,050 --> 01:35:32,800
What you think is scarcely the point.

920
01:35:33,060 --> 01:35:36,810
It's what His Majesty thinks that counts.

921
01:35:37,140 --> 01:35:39,190
But, Your Majesty

922
01:35:39,400 --> 01:35:41,270
Mozart...

923
01:35:41,480 --> 01:35:43,690
I am a tolerant man.

924
01:35:43,900 --> 01:35:48,820
I do not censor things lightly. When I do, I have good reason.

925
01:35:49,700 --> 01:35:52,700
Figaro is a bad play.

926
01:35:53,330 --> 01:35:55,990
It stirs up hatred between classes.

927
01:35:56,250 --> 01:35:59,290
In France, it has caused only bitterness.

928
01:35:59,500 --> 01:36:04,840
My sister Antoinette is beginning to be frightened of her own people.

929
01:36:05,000 --> 01:36:08,630
I swear, there's nothing like that in the piece.

930
01:36:08,840 --> 01:36:13,760
I've taken out everything that could give offense. I hate politics.

931
01:36:13,970 --> 01:36:16,510
I'm afraid you're rather innocent.

932
01:36:16,720 --> 01:36:21,850
In these dangerous times I cannot afford to provoke our people...

933
01:36:22,020 --> 01:36:24,360
simply over a theater piece.

934
01:36:24,610 --> 01:36:29,650
Majesty, this is just a frolic. A piece about love.

935
01:36:29,860 --> 01:36:31,860
"Love." Again!

936
01:36:32,240 --> 01:36:33,870
And it's new!

937
01:36:34,120 --> 01:36:38,160
It's entirely new. The people will go mad for it.

938
01:36:38,370 --> 01:36:40,620
I have scenes....

939
01:36:41,370 --> 01:36:43,880
The end of Act II, for example.

940
01:36:44,040 --> 01:36:48,050
It starts as a duet. A husband and wife quarreling.

941
01:36:48,300 --> 01:36:53,380
Suddenly, the scheming maid comes in. It's a very funny situation.

942
01:36:53,640 --> 01:36:55,470
Duet turns into trio.

943
01:36:55,680 --> 01:36:58,560
Then the husband's valet comes in.

944
01:36:58,770 --> 01:37:00,560
Trio turns into quartet.

945
01:37:00,770 --> 01:37:03,730
Then a gardener. Quartet becomes quintet.

946
01:37:03,900 --> 01:37:05,900
And so on, on and on.

947
01:37:06,150 --> 01:37:08,730
Sextet, septet, octet.

948
01:37:08,900 --> 01:37:12,700
How long do you think I can sustain that?

949
01:37:13,490 --> 01:37:14,910
I have no idea.

950
01:37:15,160 --> 01:37:16,530
Guess.

951
01:37:17,490 --> 01:37:18,910
Guess, Your Majesty.

952
01:37:19,160 --> 01:37:24,170
Imagine the longest time it could be sustained, then double it.

953
01:37:25,000 --> 01:37:29,590
Well....Six...

954
01:37:30,420 --> 01:37:32,720
seven minutes?

955
01:37:35,430 --> 01:37:39,850
-Eight minutes? -Twenty, sire. Twenty minutes!

956
01:37:40,060 --> 01:37:44,390
Twenty minutes of continuous music. No recitatives!

957
01:37:44,850 --> 01:37:47,230
Sire, only opera can do this.

958
01:37:47,440 --> 01:37:51,360
In a play, if more than one person speaks at once...

959
01:37:51,570 --> 01:37:53,530
it's just noise.

960
01:37:53,740 --> 01:37:56,280
But with opera, with music...

961
01:37:56,450 --> 01:38:00,620
you can have 20 individuals all talking at the same time.

962
01:38:00,870 --> 01:38:03,870
It's not noise. It's a perfect harmony!

963
01:38:04,290 --> 01:38:07,420
Mozart, music is not the issue here.

964
01:38:07,630 --> 01:38:12,920
No one doubts your talent. It's your literary judgment that's in question.

965
01:38:13,130 --> 01:38:19,140
Even without the politics, it would remain a vulgar farce.

966
01:38:19,390 --> 01:38:22,220
Why waste your spirit on such rubbish?

967
01:38:22,430 --> 01:38:26,480
Surely you can choose more elevated themes.

968
01:38:26,650 --> 01:38:29,860
Elevated! What does that mean, elevated?

969
01:38:30,070 --> 01:38:33,820
I am fed to the teeth with these...

970
01:38:33,990 --> 01:38:37,280
elevated things. Old dead legends.

971
01:38:37,490 --> 01:38:41,620
Why must we go on forever writing of gods and legends?

972
01:38:41,830 --> 01:38:46,830
Because they do. They go on forever.

973
01:38:47,580 --> 01:38:51,500
At least what they represent: the eternal in us.

974
01:38:51,750 --> 01:38:54,510
Opera is here to ennoble us, Mozart.

975
01:38:54,670 --> 01:38:57,800
You and me, just the same as His Majesty.

976
01:38:58,010 --> 01:39:01,350
Bello. Veramente.

977
01:39:02,100 --> 01:39:06,850
"Bello, bello, bello." Come on now, be honest!

978
01:39:07,020 --> 01:39:12,690
You'd rather listen to your hairdresser than Hercules, Horatius or Orpheus.

979
01:39:12,940 --> 01:39:16,990
People so lofty, they sound as if they shit marble!

980
01:39:17,780 --> 01:39:19,490
What!

981
01:39:19,870 --> 01:39:23,910
Govern your tongue, Mozart! How dare you!

982
01:39:28,370 --> 01:39:31,210
Forgive me, Majesty.

983
01:39:32,420 --> 01:39:34,840
I'm a vulgar man...

984
01:39:35,050 --> 01:39:38,220
but I assure you, my music is not.

985
01:39:41,890 --> 01:39:45,060
You are passionate, Mozart...

986
01:39:45,310 --> 01:39:49,230
but you do not persuade.

987
01:39:51,730 --> 01:39:55,570
Sire, the whole opera is finished.

988
01:39:55,860 --> 01:39:59,070
Do you know how much work went into it?

989
01:39:59,410 --> 01:40:04,740
His Majesty has been more than patient, signore.

990
01:40:05,910 --> 01:40:09,160
How can I persuade if I can't show it?

991
01:40:09,370 --> 01:40:12,420
That will do, Herr Mozart.

992
01:40:14,250 --> 01:40:17,170
Just let me tell you how it begins.

993
01:40:17,380 --> 01:40:21,260
May I just do that, Majesty? Show you how it begins? Just that?

994
01:40:26,770 --> 01:40:28,100
Please.

995
01:40:29,100 --> 01:40:30,940
Look....

996
01:40:31,230 --> 01:40:34,690
There's a servant on his knees. Do you know why?

997
01:40:34,900 --> 01:40:38,280
Not from oppression. He's measuring a space.

998
01:40:38,530 --> 01:40:40,570
Do you know what for?

999
01:40:40,780 --> 01:40:43,490
His bed. His wedding bed.

1000
01:40:43,700 --> 01:40:45,990
To see if it will fit!

1001
01:41:19,820 --> 01:41:23,570
Well, Mozart is already rehearsing.

1002
01:41:28,660 --> 01:41:31,910
In that case, gentlemen, I think....

1003
01:41:36,040 --> 01:41:39,170
I think we should help Mozart all we can.

1004
01:41:42,470 --> 01:41:45,680
And protect him against the emperor's anger.

1005
01:41:45,930 --> 01:41:47,800
What anger?

1006
01:41:48,010 --> 01:41:50,260
About the ballet.

1007
01:41:50,970 --> 01:41:53,310
What ballet?

1008
01:41:53,770 --> 01:42:01,360
Excuse me...but didn't His Majesty specifically forbid the ballet in his opera?

1009
01:42:36,230 --> 01:42:37,650
Mozart!

1010
01:42:38,480 --> 01:42:40,820
-Herr Mozart! -Yes?

1011
01:42:41,020 --> 01:42:44,150
-A word with you.  Certainly, Herr Direktor.

1012
01:42:44,360 --> 01:42:46,240
Now, Herr Mozart!

1013
01:42:47,200 --> 01:42:49,070
Five minutes, please.

1014
01:42:49,240 --> 01:42:50,620
Five minutes!

1015
01:42:52,240 --> 01:42:53,490
Yes?

1016
01:42:53,700 --> 01:42:59,420
Do you not know that His Majesty has expressly forbidden ballet in operas?

1017
01:42:59,670 --> 01:43:04,590
-It's not a ballet, it's a dance. -Exactly. A dance.

1018
01:43:04,760 --> 01:43:09,430
Surely, His Majesty didn't mean no dancing when it's in the story.

1019
01:43:09,680 --> 01:43:15,140
It's dangerous to interpret his edicts. Give me your score, please.

1020
01:43:24,030 --> 01:43:25,740
Thank you.

1021
01:43:28,910 --> 01:43:31,910
What are you doing, Herr Direktor?

1022
01:43:32,120 --> 01:43:35,750
Taking out what you should never have put in.

1023
01:43:36,870 --> 01:43:39,580
Please. Please!

1024
01:43:39,960 --> 01:43:42,420
I have no one else to turn to.

1025
01:43:42,630 --> 01:43:45,300
-What is it? -It's unbelievable.

1026
01:43:45,460 --> 01:43:49,680
The direktor has torn up a huge section of my music.

1027
01:43:49,890 --> 01:43:53,100
They say I have to rewrite the opera.

1028
01:43:53,720 --> 01:43:56,220
But it's perfect as it is.

1029
01:43:56,430 --> 01:43:57,680
I can't...

1030
01:43:57,890 --> 01:44:00,480
rewrite what's perfect.

1031
01:44:02,270 --> 01:44:03,650
Please.

1032
01:44:03,820 --> 01:44:06,230
Can't you talk to him?

1033
01:44:06,740 --> 01:44:07,990
Please.

1034
01:44:08,200 --> 01:44:10,990
Why bother? He's no friend of yours.

1035
01:44:11,200 --> 01:44:14,910
I could kill him! I mean, really! Kill him!

1036
01:44:16,910 --> 01:44:21,000
I threw the entire score into the fire, he made me so angry.

1037
01:44:21,250 --> 01:44:26,500
-You burned the score? -No, my wife took it out in time.

1038
01:44:28,130 --> 01:44:29,510
Thank God.

1039
01:44:31,220 --> 01:44:36,260
It's unfair that a man like that should have power over our work!

1040
01:44:37,600 --> 01:44:40,980
But there are those who have power over him.

1041
01:44:42,650 --> 01:44:46,020
I think I'll take this up with the emperor.

1042
01:44:47,940 --> 01:44:49,440
Excellency...

1043
01:44:49,650 --> 01:44:50,860
would you?

1044
01:44:52,530 --> 01:44:55,450
With all my heart, Mozart.

1045
01:44:56,540 --> 01:44:59,040
Thank you.

1046
01:44:59,250 --> 01:45:04,210
Please, Herr Mozart. "Please, it's not a holy relic."

1047
01:45:06,380 --> 01:45:11,170
I don't need to tell you I said nothing, whatever, to the emperor.

1048
01:45:11,380 --> 01:45:16,050
I went to the theater to tell Mozart something, anything...

1049
01:45:17,560 --> 01:45:22,310
when suddenly, in the middle of the third act...

1050
01:45:22,520 --> 01:45:30,480
to my astonishment, the emperor...who never attended rehearsals, suddenly appeared.

1051
01:45:49,170 --> 01:45:51,300
What is this?

1052
01:45:53,760 --> 01:45:55,720
I don't understand.

1053
01:45:56,760 --> 01:45:58,180
Is it modern?

1054
01:45:59,220 --> 01:46:00,930
Majesty...

1055
01:46:01,180 --> 01:46:02,890
the Herr Direktor...

1056
01:46:03,100 --> 01:46:10,690
he has removed un balletto...that would have occurred at this place.

1057
01:46:11,690 --> 01:46:13,110
Why?

1058
01:46:13,450 --> 01:46:15,610
It is your regulation, sire.

1059
01:46:15,820 --> 01:46:18,870
No ballet in your opera.

1060
01:46:24,620 --> 01:46:26,370
Salieri.

1061
01:46:27,750 --> 01:46:29,460
Do you like this?

1062
01:46:31,880 --> 01:46:35,630
It's not a question of liking, Majesty.

1063
01:46:35,880 --> 01:46:38,930
Your own law decrees it, I'm afraid.

1064
01:46:40,640 --> 01:46:42,930
Well, look at them!

1065
01:46:45,060 --> 01:46:48,270
No! This is nonsense!

1066
01:46:48,480 --> 01:46:52,480
-Let me see the scene with the music. -But, sire!

1067
01:46:52,730 --> 01:46:54,150
Oblige me!

1068
01:46:54,400 --> 01:46:56,450
Yes, Majesty.

1069
01:47:05,500 --> 01:47:08,790
Can we see the scene with the music, please?

1070
01:47:09,000 --> 01:47:12,340
Certainly! Certainly, Herr Direktor!

1071
01:47:17,930 --> 01:47:20,680
Bring the palace set back in, please.

1072
01:47:58,720 --> 01:48:03,050
The restored third act...was bold, brilliant.

1073
01:48:03,930 --> 01:48:05,930
The fourth...

1074
01:48:08,390 --> 01:48:10,350
was astounding.

1075
01:48:18,400 --> 01:48:19,860
I saw a woman...

1076
01:48:20,070 --> 01:48:25,870
disguised in her maid's clothes hear her husband speak the first...

1077
01:48:26,080 --> 01:48:29,500
tender words he has offered her in years.

1078
01:48:29,710 --> 01:48:34,420
Simply because he thinks she is someone else.

1079
01:48:35,090 --> 01:48:40,550
I heard the music of true forgiveness filling the theater...

1080
01:48:40,760 --> 01:48:45,260
conferring on all who sat there, perfect absolution.

1081
01:48:46,010 --> 01:48:49,180
God was singing through this little man...

1082
01:48:49,390 --> 01:48:51,940
to all the world.

1083
01:48:52,560 --> 01:48:54,520
Unstoppable.

1084
01:48:54,730 --> 01:49:00,110
Making my defeat more bitter with every passing bar.

1085
01:49:38,320 --> 01:49:41,110
And then, do you know what happened?

1086
01:49:44,280 --> 01:49:45,820
A miracle!

1087
01:49:52,960 --> 01:49:54,330
With that yawn...

1088
01:49:54,750 --> 01:49:58,670
I saw my defeat turn into a victory.

1089
01:50:02,510 --> 01:50:06,300
Mozart was lucky the emperor yawned only once.

1090
01:50:06,510 --> 01:50:07,970
Three yawns...

1091
01:50:08,180 --> 01:50:11,180
and the opera would fail the same night.

1092
01:50:11,430 --> 01:50:14,770
Two yawns, within a week at most.

1093
01:50:14,980 --> 01:50:19,940
With one yawn, the composer could still get....

1094
01:50:21,650 --> 01:50:26,450
Nine performances! Nine! That's all it's had! Withdrawn!

1095
01:50:26,660 --> 01:50:28,950
I know, I know.

1096
01:50:29,200 --> 01:50:30,950
It's outrageous.

1097
01:50:32,580 --> 01:50:36,330
Still, if the public doesn't like one's work...

1098
01:50:36,670 --> 01:50:39,210
one has to accept the fact gracefully.

1099
01:50:39,380 --> 01:50:42,460
But what is it that they don't like?

1100
01:50:43,010 --> 01:50:45,380
I can speak for the emperor.

1101
01:50:45,590 --> 01:50:48,800
You make too many demands on the royal ear.

1102
01:50:49,010 --> 01:50:54,350
The poor man can't concentrate for more than an hour. You gave him four.

1103
01:50:59,650 --> 01:51:02,480
What did you think of it yourself?

1104
01:51:02,690 --> 01:51:05,190
Did you like it at all?

1105
01:51:06,740 --> 01:51:09,370
I thought it was marvelous.

1106
01:51:09,620 --> 01:51:13,240
Of course. It's the best opera yet written.

1107
01:51:13,580 --> 01:51:15,160
I know it!

1108
01:51:18,040 --> 01:51:19,750
Why didn't they come?

1109
01:51:22,630 --> 01:51:26,340
I think you overestimate our dear Viennese, friend.

1110
01:51:26,550 --> 01:51:30,050
You didn't give them a bang at the end of songs...

1111
01:51:30,260 --> 01:51:32,720
to let them know when to clap.

1112
01:51:33,430 --> 01:51:35,930
I know, I know.

1113
01:51:36,140 --> 01:51:39,600
Maybe you should give me some lessons in that.

1114
01:51:40,650 --> 01:51:43,150
I wouldn't presume.

1115
01:51:46,280 --> 01:51:49,280
Nevertheless, at the risk of imposing...

1116
01:51:49,530 --> 01:51:52,530
I'd like you to see my new piece.

1117
01:51:53,790 --> 01:51:55,950
It would be an honor for me.

1118
01:51:56,200 --> 01:51:58,870
No, the honor would be all mine.

1119
01:53:25,040 --> 01:53:29,880
I believe....I believe...

1120
01:53:30,050 --> 01:53:34,050
it is the best opera yet written, my friends.

1121
01:53:36,140 --> 01:53:37,760
Salieri!

1122
01:53:39,180 --> 01:53:43,230
You are the brightest star in the musical firmament.

1123
01:53:43,390 --> 01:53:46,900
You do honor to Vienna and to me.

1124
01:54:13,550 --> 01:54:14,930
Herr Mozart!

1125
01:54:15,800 --> 01:54:19,010
-It was good of you to come. -How could I not?

1126
01:54:22,350 --> 01:54:25,190
Did my work please you?

1127
01:54:26,600 --> 01:54:30,570
I never knew that music like that was possible.

1128
01:54:31,780 --> 01:54:34,440
-You flatter me. -No, no.

1129
01:54:35,410 --> 01:54:37,780
One hears such sounds...

1130
01:54:37,950 --> 01:54:41,410
and what can one say but: Salieri!

1131
01:54:48,790 --> 01:54:54,380
Everybody's here, and we've got guests. Bravo! I've got some more.

1132
01:54:54,590 --> 01:54:58,340
You remember my good friend Schikaneder. Come in.

1133
01:54:58,550 --> 01:54:59,850
Don't be shy.

1134
01:55:00,050 --> 01:55:04,270
-This is a very nice girl, and this -Wolfie?

1135
01:55:05,270 --> 01:55:07,310
Yes, my love?

1136
01:55:07,770 --> 01:55:11,360
-These gentlemen are from Salzburg. -Salzburg?

1137
01:55:12,610 --> 01:55:14,480
We were just talking about Salzburg.

1138
01:55:14,650 --> 01:55:16,110
Wolfie....

1139
01:55:17,780 --> 01:55:20,280
Your father is dead.

1140
01:55:42,680 --> 01:55:45,310
So rose the dreadful ghost...

1141
01:55:45,520 --> 01:55:49,900
from his next and blackest opera.

1142
01:55:55,190 --> 01:55:59,530
There on the stage, stood the figure of a dead commander.

1143
01:55:59,780 --> 01:56:01,370
I knew...

1144
01:56:01,530 --> 01:56:03,330
only I understood...

1145
01:56:03,530 --> 01:56:08,710
that the horrifying apparition was Leopold...raised from the dead!

1146
01:56:38,320 --> 01:56:42,320
Wolfgang had actually summoned up his own father...

1147
01:56:42,530 --> 01:56:46,240
to accuse his son before all the world!

1148
01:56:47,580 --> 01:56:49,450
It was...

1149
01:56:49,660 --> 01:56:53,080
terrifying and wonderful to watch.

1150
01:57:57,150 --> 01:57:58,650
And now...

1151
01:58:04,160 --> 01:58:07,280
the madness began in me.

1152
01:58:09,540 --> 01:58:13,080
The madness of a man splitting in half.

1153
01:58:16,580 --> 01:58:19,290
Through my influence, I saw to it...

1154
01:58:19,500 --> 01:58:23,340
Don Giovanni was played only five times in Vienna.

1155
01:58:23,590 --> 01:58:28,180
But, in secret, I went to every one of those five.

1156
01:58:28,430 --> 01:58:33,350
Worshiping sound I alone seemed to hear.

1157
01:59:20,020 --> 01:59:23,480
And as I stood there, understanding how...

1158
01:59:23,690 --> 01:59:27,240
that bitter old man was still possessing his poor son...

1159
01:59:27,490 --> 01:59:30,160
even from beyond the grave...

1160
01:59:30,410 --> 01:59:32,240
I began to see a way...

1161
01:59:32,540 --> 01:59:34,330
a terrible way...

1162
01:59:34,540 --> 01:59:39,500
I could finally triumph...over God.

1163
02:02:49,570 --> 02:02:51,270
Herr Mozart?

1164
02:02:54,240 --> 02:02:57,360
I have come to commission work from you.

1165
02:02:58,740 --> 02:03:03,120
-What work? -A Mass for the dead.

1166
02:03:03,330 --> 02:03:05,290
What dead?

1167
02:03:05,710 --> 02:03:07,790
Who is dead?

1168
02:03:07,960 --> 02:03:12,630
A man who deserved a Requiem Mass and never got one.

1169
02:03:12,880 --> 02:03:16,420
-Who are you? -I am only a messenger.

1170
02:03:16,630 --> 02:03:18,840
Do you accept?

1171
02:03:19,140 --> 02:03:21,550
You will be well paid.

1172
02:03:29,110 --> 02:03:31,360
Do you accept?

1173
02:03:41,950 --> 02:03:43,410
Work fast.

1174
02:03:43,620 --> 02:03:46,370
And be sure tell no one what you do.

1175
02:03:46,580 --> 02:03:49,080
You will see me again soon.

1176
02:04:38,170 --> 02:04:41,010
My plan was so simple...

1177
02:04:42,050 --> 02:04:44,550
that it terrified me.

1178
02:04:46,640 --> 02:04:50,560
First, I must get the death Mass, and then...

1179
02:04:52,560 --> 02:04:55,570
I must achieve his death.

1180
02:04:57,070 --> 02:04:58,740
What?

1181
02:04:59,570 --> 02:05:01,700
His funeral!

1182
02:05:02,530 --> 02:05:03,820
Imagine it!

1183
02:05:04,030 --> 02:05:07,080
The cathedral, all Vienna sitting there.

1184
02:05:07,370 --> 02:05:12,710
His coffin. Mozart's little coffin in the middle.

1185
02:05:13,380 --> 02:05:15,080
And then...

1186
02:05:15,750 --> 02:05:18,000
in that silence...

1187
02:05:20,170 --> 02:05:22,090
music.

1188
02:05:23,430 --> 02:05:25,720
A divine music...

1189
02:05:25,930 --> 02:05:28,850
bursts out over them all.

1190
02:05:29,480 --> 02:05:33,190
A great Mass of death.

1191
02:05:34,480 --> 02:05:38,440
Requiem Mass for Wolfgang Mozart.

1192
02:05:38,610 --> 02:05:42,900
Composed by his devoted friend...

1193
02:05:43,280 --> 02:05:46,070
Antonio Salieri.

1194
02:05:47,030 --> 02:05:48,740
What sublimity!

1195
02:05:48,950 --> 02:05:51,540
What depth!

1196
02:05:51,750 --> 02:05:54,790
What passion in the music!

1197
02:05:55,540 --> 02:05:59,460
Salieri has been touched by God at last...

1198
02:05:59,630 --> 02:06:02,300
and God forced to listen!

1199
02:06:03,760 --> 02:06:07,300
Powerless to stop it!

1200
02:06:07,510 --> 02:06:10,970
I, for once, in the end, laughing at him!

1201
02:06:18,400 --> 02:06:22,650
The only thing that worried me was the actual killing.

1202
02:06:22,900 --> 02:06:25,280
How does one do that?

1203
02:06:26,030 --> 02:06:28,830
How does one kill a man?

1204
02:06:30,040 --> 02:06:32,040
It's one thing...

1205
02:06:32,250 --> 02:06:34,620
to dream about it.

1206
02:06:34,830 --> 02:06:38,080
Very different when you....

1207
02:06:40,420 --> 02:06:42,800
When you have to do it...

1208
02:06:45,340 --> 02:06:47,800
with your own hands.

1209
02:06:57,310 --> 02:07:00,110
Come in!

1210
02:07:15,660 --> 02:07:20,210
I've come to dinner

1211
02:07:20,420 --> 02:07:23,210
Dinner! Are you mad? I'm a nobleman!

1212
02:07:23,420 --> 02:07:26,880
I only ever dine with people of my own height!

1213
02:07:27,130 --> 02:07:28,890
Stop it!

1214
02:07:29,550 --> 02:07:31,680
Be careful Be careful

1215
02:07:31,890 --> 02:07:34,770
Hold tight

1216
02:07:35,270 --> 02:07:37,560
I'm a famous...

1217
02:07:37,730 --> 02:07:40,560
horseman

1218
02:07:40,730 --> 02:07:45,070
And we're a famous horsy

1219
02:07:47,070 --> 02:07:51,070
Give me a hoof, my darling

1220
02:07:51,240 --> 02:07:56,410
And I'll give you my heart

1221
02:07:56,660 --> 02:08:01,170
Take me to your stable

1222
02:08:01,380 --> 02:08:04,670
And nevermore we'll part

1223
02:08:11,760 --> 02:08:14,760
Kill me Kill me

1224
02:08:36,120 --> 02:08:40,960
We're going to make a soprano stew

1225
02:08:41,130 --> 02:08:45,800
We're going to make a soprano stew

1226
02:08:46,000 --> 02:08:49,800
And when you make a soprano stew

1227
02:08:49,970 --> 02:08:51,840
Shut up!

1228
02:08:52,090 --> 02:08:54,800
I'm sick to death of that tune!

1229
02:09:13,740 --> 02:09:17,330
Give me some hay, my darling

1230
02:09:17,540 --> 02:09:21,120
And I'll give you my heart

1231
02:09:21,330 --> 02:09:23,500
Leporello! Some hay!

1232
02:10:14,380 --> 02:10:16,510
We hope...

1233
02:10:16,720 --> 02:10:20,890
you're contented

1234
02:10:22,180 --> 02:10:24,810
With what...

1235
02:10:25,020 --> 02:10:29,190
we've presented

1236
02:10:30,030 --> 02:10:36,700
And love our dove of peace

1237
02:10:37,120 --> 02:10:43,870
And love...

1238
02:10:44,080 --> 02:10:48,080
our dove of peace

1239
02:11:01,890 --> 02:11:04,600
-What did you think? -It was wonderful!

1240
02:11:04,850 --> 02:11:09,060
-He liked the little people. -It's all in good fun.

1241
02:11:10,230 --> 02:11:12,440
I liked the horse.

1242
02:11:23,410 --> 02:11:27,000
I tell you, if you played Don Giovanni here...

1243
02:11:27,460 --> 02:11:30,460
you would've had a wonderful success.

1244
02:11:30,630 --> 02:11:32,420
You belong here.

1245
02:11:32,630 --> 02:11:36,800
Not at the snobby court. You could do anything you like.

1246
02:11:37,010 --> 02:11:41,800
The more fantastic, the better. That's what people want: fantasy.

1247
02:11:42,010 --> 02:11:45,270
You write a proper part for me...

1248
02:11:45,480 --> 02:11:47,770
a couple of catchy songs...

1249
02:11:47,980 --> 02:11:52,320
I guarantee you a triumph deluxe!

1250
02:11:52,980 --> 02:11:57,110
-What do you say? -How much will you pay him?

1251
02:11:57,320 --> 02:11:58,820
Ah!

1252
02:11:58,990 --> 02:12:02,620
Well! I see you brought your manager with you.

1253
02:12:04,490 --> 02:12:06,620
Well, madame...

1254
02:12:06,830 --> 02:12:10,000
how about half the receipts?

1255
02:12:10,420 --> 02:12:12,000
Half the receipts!

1256
02:12:12,170 --> 02:12:14,500
-Stanzi! -I'm talking about now.

1257
02:12:14,710 --> 02:12:18,170
How much will you pay him now? Down payment.

1258
02:12:18,430 --> 02:12:20,430
Down payment?

1259
02:12:21,510 --> 02:12:25,010
Who do you think I am, the emperor?

1260
02:12:25,220 --> 02:12:27,520
Whoops. I have to go.

1261
02:12:27,730 --> 02:12:30,850
Stay here, you'll enjoy this next one.

1262
02:12:32,440 --> 02:12:33,810
You won't do this.

1263
02:12:34,020 --> 02:12:36,360
-Why not? Half the house! -When?

1264
02:12:36,570 --> 02:12:40,660
We need money now! He pays you now, or you don't do it.

1265
02:12:40,860 --> 02:12:42,490
I don't trust that man.

1266
02:12:42,700 --> 02:12:46,330
I don't like what he did with your opera. It was common.

1267
02:12:46,540 --> 02:12:49,540
You liked it. Monkey, punky, flunky!

1268
02:12:49,710 --> 02:12:51,250
Half the house.

1269
02:12:51,500 --> 02:12:55,540
You'll never see a penny. I want it here in my hand.

1270
02:12:55,750 --> 02:12:59,470
-I'll put it here in your hand. -Shut up!

1271
02:12:59,680 --> 02:13:03,590
You won't put a thing in my hand until I see some money!

1272
02:13:04,890 --> 02:13:09,480
It's embarrassing. Can't you think of anyone who can do something for him?

1273
02:13:10,100 --> 02:13:14,060
I'm afraid Mozart is a lost cause, baron.

1274
02:13:14,610 --> 02:13:18,900
He has succeeded in alienating practically the whole of Vienna.

1275
02:13:19,070 --> 02:13:20,990
He never pays his debts.

1276
02:13:21,200 --> 02:13:25,240
I can't think of anyone to whom I'd dare recommend him.

1277
02:13:25,410 --> 02:13:29,700
Herr Mozart. What a surprise!

1278
02:13:30,790 --> 02:13:33,080
What can I do for you?

1279
02:13:34,420 --> 02:13:38,920
Is my pupil still interested in learning the art of music?

1280
02:13:40,510 --> 02:13:45,300
Your pupil is married and living in Mannheim, young man.

1281
02:13:45,930 --> 02:13:47,600
Really?

1282
02:13:53,100 --> 02:13:58,770
Perhaps your dear wife might care to profit from my instruction.

1283
02:13:59,230 --> 02:14:01,530
What is it, Mozart?

1284
02:14:01,740 --> 02:14:04,410
What's the matter with you?

1285
02:14:04,610 --> 02:14:11,160
Well ...since it appears no one is eager to hire my services...

1286
02:14:11,410 --> 02:14:15,120
could you favor me with a little money instead?

1287
02:14:18,170 --> 02:14:19,630
What for?

1288
02:14:21,170 --> 02:14:25,340
If a man cannot earn, he must borrow.

1289
02:14:28,760 --> 02:14:31,810
That's hardly the way to go about it.

1290
02:14:32,770 --> 02:14:36,150
You are right, sir. You are right.

1291
02:14:36,310 --> 02:14:40,820
But you see, I am endowed with talent, and you with money.

1292
02:14:40,980 --> 02:14:42,940
If I offer mine...

1293
02:14:43,150 --> 02:14:45,820
you should offer yours.

1294
02:14:48,990 --> 02:14:51,160
I'm sorry, no.

1295
02:14:53,960 --> 02:14:55,620
Please.

1296
02:14:57,500 --> 02:15:00,090
My answer is no, Mozart.

1297
02:15:06,300 --> 02:15:08,180
Please.

1298
02:15:12,390 --> 02:15:14,600
Please!

1299
02:15:51,430 --> 02:15:53,560
Don't answer it.

1300
02:15:55,430 --> 02:15:57,140
Why?

1301
02:15:59,350 --> 02:16:01,060
Tell him....

1302
02:16:02,190 --> 02:16:04,400
Tell him I'm not here.

1303
02:16:04,780 --> 02:16:06,740
Tell him....

1304
02:16:07,740 --> 02:16:10,240
Tell him I'm working on it.

1305
02:16:11,240 --> 02:16:13,410
Come back later.

1306
02:16:29,550 --> 02:16:32,470
Am I interrupting?  No.

1307
02:16:32,760 --> 02:16:35,600
Good. Where's our friend?

1308
02:16:35,770 --> 02:16:37,770
He's not here.

1309
02:16:38,270 --> 02:16:41,770
But he's working on it, he told me to tell you.

1310
02:16:42,730 --> 02:16:44,690
Is that it?

1311
02:16:50,490 --> 02:16:52,990
Is he happy with it?

1312
02:16:55,990 --> 02:16:59,000
What's this? A Requiem Mass?

1313
02:16:59,250 --> 02:17:03,460
-You think I'm in the funeral business? -Leave that alone!

1314
02:17:03,630 --> 02:17:08,010
-Put it down! It's not for you! -I'm sorry.

1315
02:17:08,420 --> 02:17:10,420
What have you got for me?

1316
02:17:11,430 --> 02:17:13,010
Finished?

1317
02:17:14,430 --> 02:17:19,100
What? -The vaudeville, what do you think?

1318
02:17:19,640 --> 02:17:21,140
Yes.

1319
02:17:21,520 --> 02:17:23,730
-Can I see it? -No.

1320
02:17:25,150 --> 02:17:26,940
Why not?

1321
02:17:27,150 --> 02:17:29,780
Because there's nothing to see.

1322
02:17:38,120 --> 02:17:39,660
Look...

1323
02:17:40,620 --> 02:17:46,630
I asked you if we could start rehearsals next week and you said yes.

1324
02:17:47,880 --> 02:17:52,260
-Well, we can. -So let me see it. Where is it?

1325
02:17:53,050 --> 02:17:54,760
Here.

1326
02:17:55,680 --> 02:18:01,180
It's all right here in my noodle. The rest is just scribbling.

1327
02:18:01,390 --> 02:18:05,190
Scribbling and bibbling. Bibbling and scribbling.

1328
02:18:08,190 --> 02:18:10,690
-Like a drink? -Look, you little clown!

1329
02:18:10,900 --> 02:18:13,570
Do you know how many people I've hired?

1330
02:18:13,820 --> 02:18:16,280
-Leave him alone! -I'm paying them!

1331
02:18:16,530 --> 02:18:20,830
-He's doing his best. -Paying them to wait. It's ridiculous!

1332
02:18:21,040 --> 02:18:23,830
You know what's ridiculous? Your libretto!

1333
02:18:24,040 --> 02:18:25,040
Oh!

1334
02:18:25,210 --> 02:18:27,880
Only an idiot would ask him to work on that!

1335
02:18:28,090 --> 02:18:30,670
Twelve-foot snakes, magic flutes?

1336
02:18:30,880 --> 02:18:33,720
What's so intelligent about a Requiem?

1337
02:18:33,930 --> 02:18:36,890
Money. Money.

1338
02:18:39,810 --> 02:18:41,560
You're mad.

1339
02:18:42,230 --> 02:18:43,680
She's mad.

1340
02:18:44,060 --> 02:18:48,230
-Oh, yes? -Wolfie, write it down.

1341
02:18:48,440 --> 02:18:50,400
Just write it down.

1342
02:18:50,570 --> 02:18:52,690
On paper.

1343
02:18:52,900 --> 02:18:56,070
It's no use to anybody in your head.

1344
02:18:56,240 --> 02:19:00,120
To hell with your death Mass!

1345
02:19:00,830 --> 02:19:03,580
Calm yourself. What's the matter with you?

1346
02:19:03,830 --> 02:19:07,120
-I won't work there anymore. -What happened?

1347
02:19:08,380 --> 02:19:11,420
You don't know what it's like.

1348
02:19:11,590 --> 02:19:14,630
Herr Mozart frightens me.

1349
02:19:14,880 --> 02:19:16,630
He drinks all day...

1350
02:19:16,890 --> 02:19:20,600
then takes all that medicine and it makes him worse.

1351
02:19:20,760 --> 02:19:22,260
Is he working?

1352
02:19:24,060 --> 02:19:27,140
Oh, I am frightened, sir, really!

1353
02:19:27,400 --> 02:19:32,270
-When he speaks, he makes no sense. -Is he working?

1354
02:19:34,150 --> 02:19:36,450
I suppose so.

1355
02:19:36,950 --> 02:19:41,620
He sits there all the time, doing some silly opera.

1356
02:19:41,870 --> 02:19:45,000
-Opera? -Don't ask me to go back again.

1357
02:19:45,250 --> 02:19:48,460
I'm frightened. I'm very, very frightened!

1358
02:19:48,670 --> 02:19:51,880
Are you sure it's an opera?

1359
02:21:35,360 --> 02:21:37,940
I don't have it yet.

1360
02:21:38,490 --> 02:21:41,610
Are you neglecting my request?

1361
02:21:42,280 --> 02:21:45,410
No. No, I....

1362
02:21:46,330 --> 02:21:48,620
I promise you...

1363
02:21:48,830 --> 02:21:52,830
I'll give you a wonderful piece, the best I ever

1364
02:21:56,590 --> 02:21:59,920
This is my wife, Stanzi.

1365
02:22:00,470 --> 02:22:04,090
I've been sick, but I'm all right now, aren't I?

1366
02:22:04,300 --> 02:22:06,430
Yes, sir. He's all right.

1367
02:22:06,600 --> 02:22:09,770
And he's working on it very hard.

1368
02:22:10,930 --> 02:22:14,600
Give me two more weeks. Please.

1369
02:22:14,810 --> 02:22:19,110
The sooner you finish, the greater your reward.

1370
02:22:19,360 --> 02:22:21,440
Work.

1371
02:22:30,290 --> 02:22:31,830
Wolfie.

1372
02:22:34,120 --> 02:22:37,290
I think you really are going mad.

1373
02:22:38,800 --> 02:22:43,380
You slave for that idiot actor who won't give you a penny!

1374
02:22:43,630 --> 02:22:46,390
And here, this is not a ghost!

1375
02:22:46,640 --> 02:22:50,640
This is a real man, who puts down real money.

1376
02:22:52,640 --> 02:22:55,640
Why on earth won't you finish it?

1377
02:22:56,600 --> 02:23:00,400
Can you give me one reason I can understand?

1378
02:23:02,490 --> 02:23:04,610
It's killing me.

1379
02:23:08,490 --> 02:23:10,830
You're drunk, aren't you?

1380
02:23:10,990 --> 02:23:14,040
Be honest, tell me. You've been drinking.

1381
02:23:16,830 --> 02:23:21,630
It's not fair. I worry about you all the time.

1382
02:23:22,050 --> 02:23:25,420
I do everything I can to help you.

1383
02:23:25,680 --> 02:23:30,010
And all you do is drink and talk nonsense and frighten me.

1384
02:23:30,220 --> 02:23:32,720
Go back to bed!

1385
02:23:42,030 --> 02:23:43,570
Please.

1386
02:23:44,690 --> 02:23:48,570
Let me.... Let me sit here.

1387
02:23:51,580 --> 02:23:53,700
Let me stay here with you.

1388
02:26:27,320 --> 02:26:30,070
I did it. And I was proud to do it.

1389
02:26:30,320 --> 02:26:34,240
"Leave!" I said. "Right away. Take the child with you!

1390
02:26:34,450 --> 02:26:38,950
Go to the spa and get your health back." I was shocked.

1391
02:26:39,200 --> 02:26:41,950
Shocked to my foundation when I saw her.

1392
02:26:42,210 --> 02:26:45,540
I couldn't believe my eyes, poor little thing.

1393
02:26:45,710 --> 02:26:49,210
You monster! No one exists but you, do they?

1394
02:26:49,380 --> 02:26:52,050
You and your music. I warned her.

1395
02:26:52,260 --> 02:26:55,090
"Choose a man, not a baby," I said.

1396
02:26:55,340 --> 02:27:00,470
"You marry him, you won't have a pot to piss in." You selfish thing!

1397
02:27:00,720 --> 02:27:04,640
Selfish, that's what you are. Simply selfish! Do you hear me?

1398
02:30:48,700 --> 02:30:49,990
Pick him up.

1399
02:30:50,200 --> 02:30:51,950
Pick him up!

1400
02:30:53,960 --> 02:30:56,370
Be careful. Come with me.

1401
02:30:56,630 --> 02:30:58,380
You, follow me.

1402
02:31:25,990 --> 02:31:29,660
-Is it over? -Yes, it's over. It's over.

1403
02:31:31,160 --> 02:31:32,620
Go!

1404
02:32:14,450 --> 02:32:16,200
Go, go. go.

1405
02:32:17,210 --> 02:32:19,080
Go! Go!

1406
02:32:47,990 --> 02:32:49,950
Where is your wife?

1407
02:32:53,120 --> 02:32:55,580
Where is your wife?

1408
02:32:57,910 --> 02:33:02,080
She's not well either. She went to the spa.

1409
02:33:03,460 --> 02:33:05,800
You are so good to me.

1410
02:33:06,300 --> 02:33:09,340
Truly. Thank you.

1411
02:33:09,800 --> 02:33:11,630
Please!

1412
02:33:12,340 --> 02:33:16,430
No, I mean to come to my opera.

1413
02:33:16,600 --> 02:33:21,600
You. You are the only colleague of mine who came.

1414
02:33:24,610 --> 02:33:26,440
Mozart.

1415
02:33:27,610 --> 02:33:31,320
I would never miss anything you had written.

1416
02:33:31,860 --> 02:33:35,280
-It's just a vaudeville. -No, no!

1417
02:33:35,490 --> 02:33:37,450
It's a sublime piece.

1418
02:33:38,750 --> 02:33:40,830
The grandest operone!

1419
02:33:49,970 --> 02:33:51,760
I tell you...

1420
02:33:52,260 --> 02:33:56,180
you are the greatest composer known to me.

1421
02:34:00,270 --> 02:34:01,520
Do you mean it?

1422
02:34:07,570 --> 02:34:09,400
-It's him! -Who?

1423
02:34:10,030 --> 02:34:11,690
The man.

1424
02:34:12,200 --> 02:34:13,990
He's here.

1425
02:34:17,030 --> 02:34:19,080
Tell him to go away.

1426
02:34:19,330 --> 02:34:23,580
Tell him I'm still working on it. Don't let him in.

1427
02:34:24,420 --> 02:34:26,670
No, no. Wait!

1428
02:34:26,880 --> 02:34:30,880
Ask him if he would give me some money now.

1429
02:34:31,090 --> 02:34:34,680
Tell him if he would, it will help me to finish it.

1430
02:34:53,570 --> 02:34:55,910
-Salieri? -Yes.

1431
02:34:57,830 --> 02:35:01,700
-Can we come in? -Better not. He's sleeping.

1432
02:35:02,540 --> 02:35:06,420
-He's all right, though? -Yes, he's just exhausted.

1433
02:35:06,630 --> 02:35:09,750
He became dizzy, that's all.

1434
02:35:09,960 --> 02:35:14,470
-Well, tell him we came by, won't you? -Of course.

1435
02:35:14,930 --> 02:35:18,090
Give him this. That's his share.

1436
02:35:18,970 --> 02:35:21,720
-That should cheer him up. -Indeed!

1437
02:35:21,890 --> 02:35:25,350
And now, good night to you all. It was...

1438
02:35:25,560 --> 02:35:27,440
perfection, truly.

1439
02:35:27,650 --> 02:35:29,110
Thank you.

1440
02:35:39,740 --> 02:35:41,580
What happened?

1441
02:35:49,960 --> 02:35:52,630
He said to give you this.

1442
02:35:53,510 --> 02:35:56,800
And if you finish by tomorrow night...

1443
02:35:57,760 --> 02:36:00,760
he will pay you another hundred ducats.

1444
02:36:01,430 --> 02:36:02,930
Another...?

1445
02:36:03,770 --> 02:36:06,810
That's too soon. Tomorrow night....

1446
02:36:08,600 --> 02:36:10,520
It's impossible.

1447
02:36:13,900 --> 02:36:16,940
-Did he say a hundred? -Yes.

1448
02:36:22,530 --> 02:36:24,490
It's too soon.

1449
02:36:26,790 --> 02:36:28,500
Can I...?

1450
02:36:28,960 --> 02:36:30,960
Could I help you?

1451
02:36:33,550 --> 02:36:35,420
Would you?

1452
02:36:39,130 --> 02:36:40,640
Actually, you could.

1453
02:36:48,230 --> 02:36:50,810
-I want to go. -Where?

1454
02:36:51,150 --> 02:36:54,360
-I want to go back to Vienna.  Now?

1455
02:36:54,570 --> 02:36:56,150
Yes. Why?

1456
02:36:58,570 --> 02:37:00,320
I feel wrong.

1457
02:37:01,870 --> 02:37:04,370
I feel wrong being here.

1458
02:37:07,250 --> 02:37:10,870
-Where did I stop? -The end of the Recordare.

1459
02:37:11,080 --> 02:37:12,710
So now Confutatis....

1460
02:37:19,590 --> 02:37:22,010
How would you translate that?

1461
02:37:22,180 --> 02:37:25,010
"Consigned to flames of woe."

1462
02:37:27,180 --> 02:37:29,890
-Do you believe in it? -What?

1463
02:37:31,190 --> 02:37:35,230
A fire which never dies, burning you forever.

1464
02:37:36,570 --> 02:37:37,860
Oh, yes.

1465
02:37:39,530 --> 02:37:41,200
Possible.

1466
02:37:42,870 --> 02:37:46,700
-Come, let's begin. -We ended in F major.

1467
02:37:46,910 --> 02:37:50,250
-Yes. -So, now, A minor.

1468
02:37:58,050 --> 02:38:01,090
-A minor. -Yes.

1469
02:38:03,930 --> 02:38:06,930
Confutatis. A minor.

1470
02:38:09,220 --> 02:38:11,140
Start with the voices.

1471
02:38:11,390 --> 02:38:14,650
-Basses first. Second beat of the -Time?

1472
02:38:14,900 --> 02:38:18,440
Common time. Second beat of the first measure.

1473
02:38:19,820 --> 02:38:21,780
On A.

1474
02:38:23,660 --> 02:38:25,910
Second measure, second beat.

1475
02:38:26,660 --> 02:38:27,910
You see?

1476
02:38:28,120 --> 02:38:29,910
-Yes. G-sharp? -Of course.

1477
02:38:30,120 --> 02:38:33,410
Second beat of the third measure, on E.

1478
02:38:40,420 --> 02:38:42,760
Do you have me? Show me.

1479
02:39:02,490 --> 02:39:05,110
Good. Good.

1480
02:39:05,280 --> 02:39:06,860
Now the tenors.

1481
02:39:07,120 --> 02:39:10,330
Fourth beat of the first measure, on C.

1482
02:39:12,450 --> 02:39:15,830
Second measure, fourth beat. D.

1483
02:39:18,130 --> 02:39:20,460
-All right? -Yes, continue.

1484
02:39:20,630 --> 02:39:23,880
Second beat of the fourth measure, on F.

1485
02:39:30,680 --> 02:39:34,680
Now the orchestra. Second bassoon, bass trombones, basses.

1486
02:39:34,890 --> 02:39:37,480
Identical notes and rhythm.

1487
02:39:40,520 --> 02:39:44,740
First bassoon, tenor trombones, with the tenors.

1488
02:39:49,660 --> 02:39:53,410
-You go too fast. -Do you have it?

1489
02:39:53,660 --> 02:39:56,830
-Bassoon to trombone what? -With the tenors.

1490
02:39:57,040 --> 02:40:00,500
-Identical? -The instruments doubling the voices.

1491
02:40:00,670 --> 02:40:04,340
Trumpets and timpani. Trumpets in D. Listen.

1492
02:40:04,550 --> 02:40:07,010
-I don't understand! -Listen!

1493
02:40:07,220 --> 02:40:11,680
Trumpets in D, tonic and dominant, first and third beats.

1494
02:40:12,680 --> 02:40:14,680
It goes with the harmony

1495
02:40:21,190 --> 02:40:23,520
Yes. Yes, yes!

1496
02:40:32,700 --> 02:40:35,040
I understand. And that's all?

1497
02:40:35,250 --> 02:40:38,660
No, now for the real fire. Strings in unison.

1498
02:40:38,870 --> 02:40:41,580
Ostinato, on A. Like this:

1499
02:40:44,380 --> 02:40:46,380
Next measure is rising.

1500
02:40:48,220 --> 02:40:50,550
-Do you have it? Show me. -Yes, yes.

1501
02:40:58,230 --> 02:41:01,270
-It's wonderful! -Yes, yes. Go on.

1502
02:41:05,070 --> 02:41:06,610
Sotto voce.

1503
02:41:08,070 --> 02:41:09,990
-Write that down! -Yes, yes.

1504
02:41:10,240 --> 02:41:13,200
-Pianissimo. -Pianissimo?

1505
02:41:17,330 --> 02:41:18,950
C major.

1506
02:41:19,210 --> 02:41:23,830
Sopranos and altos in thirds. Altos on C, sopranos above.

1507
02:41:36,600 --> 02:41:39,350
-Sopranos up to F on the second voca? -Yes.

1508
02:41:39,600 --> 02:41:45,270
And on dictus. And underneath, just violins. Arpeggios.

1509
02:41:45,770 --> 02:41:49,150
Scale in eighth notes, then back to ostinato.

1510
02:41:49,360 --> 02:41:51,530
-Do you have it? -You go too fast.

1511
02:41:51,780 --> 02:41:54,990
-Do you have it? -One moment, please!

1512
02:41:57,740 --> 02:41:58,790
Yes.

1513
02:41:58,950 --> 02:42:02,790
Good. Show me the whole thing from the beginning.

1514
02:44:06,080 --> 02:44:08,580
Do you want to rest a bit?

1515
02:44:08,920 --> 02:44:11,090
No, I'm not tired at all.

1516
02:44:16,970 --> 02:44:19,760
We'll stop for a moment.

1517
02:44:19,930 --> 02:44:25,020
-Then we'll finish the Lacrimosa. -I can keep going. I assure you.

1518
02:44:25,270 --> 02:44:28,770
Will you stay with me while I sleep a little?

1519
02:44:30,270 --> 02:44:32,520
I'm not leaving you.

1520
02:44:39,990 --> 02:44:42,320
I'm so ashamed.

1521
02:44:43,620 --> 02:44:45,660
Of what?

1522
02:44:46,160 --> 02:44:48,620
I was foolish.

1523
02:44:48,790 --> 02:44:53,420
I thought you did not care for my work, or me.

1524
02:44:57,050 --> 02:44:59,010
Forgive me.

1525
02:45:03,640 --> 02:45:05,680
Forgive me.

1526
02:46:03,530 --> 02:46:05,990
What are you doing here?

1527
02:46:08,200 --> 02:46:11,370
Your husband took sick.

1528
02:46:12,540 --> 02:46:14,540
I brought him home.

1529
02:46:16,250 --> 02:46:18,050
Why you?

1530
02:46:19,210 --> 02:46:22,420
Because, madame, I was at hand.

1531
02:46:26,220 --> 02:46:29,560
Well, thank you very much. You can go now.

1532
02:46:32,060 --> 02:46:34,100
He needs me, ma'am.

1533
02:46:34,400 --> 02:46:36,270
No, he doesn't.

1534
02:46:36,520 --> 02:46:40,570
And I don't want you here. Just go, please.

1535
02:46:41,280 --> 02:46:43,320
-He asked me to stay. -And I'm ask

1536
02:47:03,090 --> 02:47:04,430
Wolfie?

1537
02:47:09,680 --> 02:47:11,850
Wolfie?

1538
02:47:14,310 --> 02:47:16,310
I'm back.

1539
02:47:19,480 --> 02:47:22,360
I missed you so much.

1540
02:47:26,110 --> 02:47:27,990
If you'd just...

1541
02:47:29,370 --> 02:47:32,370
show me that you need me.

1542
02:47:38,290 --> 02:47:41,590
And I'll try to do better too.

1543
02:47:53,310 --> 02:47:55,140
What is this?

1544
02:47:58,310 --> 02:48:02,690
No, Wolfie, not this. Not this.

1545
02:48:06,360 --> 02:48:10,160
You're not to work on this ever again.

1546
02:48:11,200 --> 02:48:13,040
I've decided.

1547
02:48:16,830 --> 02:48:19,500
This is not his handwriting.

1548
02:48:21,250 --> 02:48:23,050
It's mine.

1549
02:48:24,050 --> 02:48:26,380
I was assisting him.

1550
02:48:27,340 --> 02:48:30,510
He's not to work on this anymore.

1551
02:48:30,680 --> 02:48:32,890
-It's making him ill. -But

1552
02:48:35,680 --> 02:48:37,850
Good night.

1553
02:48:40,360 --> 02:48:44,940
I regret we have no servants to show you out, Herr Salieri.

1554
02:48:45,190 --> 02:48:48,070
Please respect my wish and go.

1555
02:48:48,360 --> 02:48:50,160
Madame...

1556
02:48:50,370 --> 02:48:52,870
I will respect his.

1557
02:48:55,200 --> 02:48:56,370
Wolfie.

1558
02:48:59,370 --> 02:49:00,540
Wolfie?

1559
02:49:05,300 --> 02:49:06,460
Wolfie?

1560
02:49:10,840 --> 02:49:11,890
Wolfie?

1561
02:49:14,810 --> 02:49:19,940
Wolfie! Wolfie!

1562
02:52:57,320 --> 02:53:00,160
Your merciful God.

1563
02:53:03,450 --> 02:53:08,790
He destroyed his own beloved, rather than let a mediocrity...

1564
02:53:08,960 --> 02:53:12,960
share in the smallest part of his glory.

1565
02:53:14,420 --> 02:53:16,000
He killed Mozart.

1566
02:53:17,010 --> 02:53:19,800
And kept me alive to torture.

1567
02:53:19,970 --> 02:53:22,140
Thirty-two years of torture.

1568
02:53:22,350 --> 02:53:28,020
Thirty-two years of slowly watching myself become extinct.

1569
02:53:28,230 --> 02:53:30,480
My music...

1570
02:53:30,690 --> 02:53:32,650
growing fainter.

1571
02:53:32,810 --> 02:53:35,650
All the time fainter...

1572
